1
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:09,718
You'll make your own dinner,
because you don't have any friends.

2
00:00:09,801 --> 00:00:12,887
- You were told, so make it.
- You make it. Yeah?

3
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:14,639
Just do what you're told.

4
00:00:15,807 --> 00:00:17,559
Hey. Make your own dinner.

5
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:19,519
You make it.

6
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:22,522
- [Nagano]<i> Here they go.</i>
- [Ruru] Bo, that's dangerous.

7
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:25,150
[both grunting]

8
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:29,320
[Ma-kun] Wait. Wait, wait.

9
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:30,447
Wait. Wait.

10
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:32,657
Okay, fine. Wait a second.

11
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:33,992
[Bo] Sorry.

12
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:36,286
They sent me flying.

13
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:37,871
[Ruru] What the actual hell?

14
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:40,206
[Assun] You okay, Maririn? So ridiculous.

15
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:42,751
Should we go to the living room for now?

16
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:44,461
- Let's go.
- Yeah, let's go.

17
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:46,671
- What about our stuff?
- [Ruru] Ladies to the living room.

18
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:49,883
That was heated. Come with us.

19
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:50,800
[Ha-chan giggles]

20
00:00:58,933 --> 00:00:59,893
Like I said…

21
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:01,019
BO (27)
COMMERCIAL PAINTER

22
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:02,312
…I'm not making his food.

23
00:01:02,812 --> 00:01:03,813
He can do it.

24
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:05,940
- Right?
- Yeah.

25
00:01:06,816 --> 00:01:08,568
Sorry, but I'm not going in there.

26
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:09,736
Right, Leo?

27
00:01:11,279 --> 00:01:13,907
[Leo] There's no way.
I don't care what they tell us.

28
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,827
That's that then.
Let's go make our own food.

29
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:22,749
I'm not forgiving him, for real.

30
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:32,967
- Isn't it cute?
- Does everyone have their own seat?

31
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:35,845
- [Assun] It's not set in stone.
- [Ruru] Yeah, it's not decided.

32
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:39,140
- Are you okay?
- [Kazu-kun] Oh, I'm fine.

33
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:40,475
- Your chain…
- [Ruru] Did you fix it?

34
00:01:40,558 --> 00:01:41,643
KAZU-KUN (29)
HOST CLUB OWNER

35
00:01:41,726 --> 00:01:43,645
- No, it's fine. Just came off.
- [Hikaru] That's good.

36
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:44,771
[Assun] Good. I was worried

37
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:46,940
- 'cause they cost millions of yen.
- Yeah, for real.

38
00:01:47,023 --> 00:01:48,358
Tell us about your past.

39
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:50,276
- Like, why are you here?
- My past?

40
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:52,529
I was married.

41
00:01:52,612 --> 00:01:53,613
Really?

42
00:01:53,696 --> 00:01:55,615
[laughter]

43
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:56,950
HA-CHAN (27)
TRAINER

44
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:58,201
[Assun] You said it so casually.

45
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:00,286
- You don't try to hide it.
- Mmm.

46
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:02,455
And how long were you married for?

47
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:04,541
- About six months.
- [Ruru] Okay.

48
00:02:04,624 --> 00:02:06,751
- Yeah.
- [Hikaru] What about kids? You have kids?

49
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:07,877
No kids?

50
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:08,795
Okay.

51
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:11,005
I kind of burned out.

52
00:02:11,089 --> 00:02:12,340
When were you married?

53
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:15,301
- Yeah, so it was last summer.
- [Ha-chan] Mmm.

54
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:16,636
- [Assun] Really?
- Around then.

55
00:02:16,719 --> 00:02:18,763
- [Ha-chan] That's recent.
- [Assun] Not that long ago.

56
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:20,181
- Yeah.
- What's your type?

57
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:21,724
[Megumi] <i>Ruru really goes for it.</i>

58
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:23,268
- Girls who are charming.
- Mmm.

59
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:24,853
It's not about having a pretty face.

60
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:27,230
Like, I don't care about that anymore.

61
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:29,399
- I totally get that.
- There's so many pretty girls.

62
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:32,527
I want a girl who can have fun with me
at a shabby<i> izakaya.</i>

63
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:34,529
- [all] Mmm.
- I totally get that.

64
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:37,490
I don't want to be with a girl
who only likes expensive restaurants,

65
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:40,535
who I have to force myself to be with.

66
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:41,911
[Nagano] <i>Look at Ruru's eyes.</i>

67
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:43,955
- Hey, what's your blood type?
- [Kazu-kun] Type O.

68
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:45,832
- What?
- [women gasp, exclaim]

69
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:47,417
- Hi, Type O.
- What's this?

70
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,002
[giggles] I'm Type O too.

71
00:02:49,085 --> 00:02:51,629
[Megumi] <i>Ruru thinks</i>
<i>he's pretty attractive, huh?</i>

72
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,132
[Leo sighs]

73
00:02:55,675 --> 00:02:58,094
LEO (25)
BAR OWNER

74
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:00,972
ARI (AGE 29)
RAPPER/MODEL

75
00:03:01,055 --> 00:03:03,182
"You go make it" is not the way to say it.

76
00:03:03,266 --> 00:03:04,851
- Did he say, "Go make it"?
- Yeah.

77
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:07,061
"Go make it 'cause you were told to."

78
00:03:08,146 --> 00:03:10,857
The hell? You say "please"
when you ask for something.

79
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:14,944
Don't skip all the steps, punk.

80
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:17,447
Washing the rice…

81
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:18,573
NAGANO

82
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:20,033
[all laugh]

83
00:03:20,116 --> 00:03:21,910
- [Bo] I'll help out.
- Huh?

84
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:23,870
- [Bo] I'll help.
- [Ma-kun] You don't have to cook.

85
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:26,831
- We'll do it today.
- [Ma-kun] Yeah.

86
00:03:26,915 --> 00:03:29,250
- You shouldn't be a burden to your bros.
- [Bo] No.

87
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:30,919
[Ari] I'll help too.

88
00:03:31,002 --> 00:03:32,795
Ari, Bo, it's okay.

89
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:34,881
Just don't think you're making it for him.

90
00:03:34,964 --> 00:03:36,132
- [Megumi] <i>So mature.</i>
- Yeah.

91
00:03:36,215 --> 00:03:38,801
- But it's not right to cause you trouble.
- [Leo] This isn't trouble.

92
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:40,136
[Bo] I'll help.

93
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:42,513
MA-KUN (28)
MMA FIGHTER

94
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:44,390
I don't want to make it. [chuckles]

95
00:03:44,974 --> 00:03:48,102
I think if he says thank you,
then I might forgive him,

96
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:49,270
just a little bit.

97
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:51,606
- Oh, he won't.
- [Leo] Only if he says thank you.

98
00:03:51,689 --> 00:03:54,943
Hey, why don't we wait
and see what his reaction is?

99
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:56,778
[Leo] If he says it, we'll forgive him.

100
00:03:56,861 --> 00:03:59,113
But if he says he doesn't want it,
I won't hold back.

101
00:04:01,616 --> 00:04:04,494
[Megumi]<i> Bo is super-efficient though,</i>
<i>with everything he does.</i>

102
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:07,205
- [Awich] <i>Yeah, that's true.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Obviously. He did it before.</i>

103
00:04:07,288 --> 00:04:09,540
[Megumi] <i>Right? He's done a lot of things.</i>

104
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:14,128
- [Maririn] Delivery.
- [Ruru] Bo, are you the waiter?

105
00:04:14,212 --> 00:04:16,422
No, I cooked the rice.
I was always gonna help.

106
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:18,383
- [Hikaru] Oh, thank you.
- [Ha-chan] Aw.

107
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:20,677
What's that?

108
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:22,095
- Pot-au-feu?
- [Ma-kun] Pot-au-feu.

109
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:24,847
- [Assun] You made pot-au-feu?
- I want to eat it.

110
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:27,767
- [Assun] I wanted to make pot-au-feu.
- [Ari] It's pot-au-feu, isn't it?

111
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:30,103
- [Leo] Taisei made it today.
- [Hikaru] Oh, really?

112
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:31,854
- [Nagano]<i> What's gonna happen?</i>
- [Leo] It's hot.

113
00:04:31,938 --> 00:04:34,482
- [Megumi]<i> What're they gonna do?</i>
- [Hikaru] Smells amazing, guys.

114
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:36,776
[Megumi]<i> Look how mad he is.</i>

115
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,444
- All right.
- Shall we eat?

116
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:39,737
- Let's eat.
- [Tai-chan] Yeah.

117
00:04:39,821 --> 00:04:40,822
Thank you, Ma-kun.

118
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:41,823
Whoa!

119
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:44,117
[chill music playing]

120
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:48,121
- [Leo] We made it together.
- Thank you, guys.

121
00:04:48,204 --> 00:04:49,956
[all] Let's eat.

122
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,083
[Nagano] <i>What just happened?</i>

123
00:04:52,166 --> 00:04:54,294
- [Awich laughs] <i>What's happening?</i>
- [Ma-kun] It's good.

124
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:56,421
- [Ha-chan] Yeah.
- [Ma-kun] It's all right, Ari.

125
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:58,923
Thanks, Taisei, that was delicious.

126
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:01,718
- No problem. Did y'all like it?
- [Ma-kun] Yeah.

127
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:03,136
[Ari] Did y'all like it?

128
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:05,054
- [Assun] Tamo-san? Like Tamo-san.
- [laughs]

129
00:05:05,138 --> 00:05:07,473
- [Megumi and Awich] <i>He's laughing!</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Wait a minute!</i>

130
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,309
- [laughs]
- Like, what just happened?

131
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:11,227
They feel what they feel in the moment.

132
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:12,812
- Just like chickens, right?
- No.

133
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:14,814
- Take a few steps, and forget.
- They're human.

134
00:05:14,897 --> 00:05:17,233
What you're witnessing
are beautiful yankii hearts.

135
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:19,319
[opening theme song playing]

136
00:05:30,246 --> 00:05:32,457
A YANKII DATING REALITY SHOW
WHERE LOVE LIVES ON THE EDGE

137
00:05:33,249 --> 00:05:35,335
RAPPER FROM SAGAMIHARA
SPITTING LYRICS OF PURE LOVE

138
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:37,003
ARI

139
00:05:37,086 --> 00:05:39,047
KAWASAKI'S IT-GIRL HOSTESS
OUT TO FIND A REAL MAN

140
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,214
HIKARU

141
00:05:40,298 --> 00:05:41,966
KYOTO BAR OWNER
GOING ALL-IN FOR HIS WOMAN

142
00:05:43,259 --> 00:05:44,886
NANIWA'S BARROOM BEAUTY
LOOKING FOR TRUE LOVE

143
00:05:44,969 --> 00:05:46,054
MARIRIN

144
00:05:46,137 --> 00:05:47,513
KURUME YANKII
WHO GREW UP BEHIND BARS

145
00:05:47,597 --> 00:05:48,723
BO

146
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:52,602
EX-YAKUZA MMA FIGHTER
LOOKING FOR HIS RIDE-OR-DIE

147
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:54,062
MA-KUN

148
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:55,938
NAGOYA'S NO.1 HOSTESS
WHO PUTS MEN IN THEIR PLACE

149
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:57,023
ASSUN

150
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:58,483
FACE-TATTOOED STYLIST
WHO LOVES HARD

151
00:05:58,566 --> 00:05:59,942
TAI-CHAN

152
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:01,235
AN HONEST MODEL
IN SEARCH OF LOVE

153
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:02,403
RURU

154
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:09,077
BRING ON THE FIGHTS
BRING ON THE LOVE

155
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,286
NO FILTER KICKBOXER
FROM MIYAGI

156
00:06:10,369 --> 00:06:11,537
HA-CHAN

157
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:12,789
EX-NO.1 HOST
CHASING TRUE LOVE

158
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:13,873
KAZU-KUN

159
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:43,820
- [PA system chiming]
- Oh, here it comes.

160
00:06:43,903 --> 00:06:46,781
- It's 'cause you just said that!
- [Ruru] Aren't I amazing?

161
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:48,991
- [Ha-chan] That's amazing.
- I told you.

162
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:51,661
- [boy on PA] <i>Everybody, it's sauna time.</i>
- [Ha-chan] Here we go.

163
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:52,954
- [Assun] Won't be Ari.
- Hikaru.

164
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:55,373
<i>The person who gets to choose is…</i>

165
00:06:55,456 --> 00:06:56,332
Please be Hikaru.

166
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:59,293
<i>…the transfer student, Kazu-kun.</i>

167
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:00,962
[Ari] Why?

168
00:07:02,088 --> 00:07:04,173
- Now?
- [Assun] Yeah, like, right now.

169
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:07,426
I choose…

170
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:09,428
Okay.

171
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:10,680
- [Nagano]<i> Ruru…</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Ooh!</i>

172
00:07:10,763 --> 00:07:11,681
- Shall we?
- Yes.

173
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:17,103
[Megumi] <i>Of course,</i>
<i>he's been locked on her since the start.</i>

174
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:23,109
[Nagano]<i> Wow.</i>

175
00:07:23,192 --> 00:07:24,902
[Megumi] <i>He's not putting his bathrobe on.</i>

176
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:26,112
[Nagano laughs]

177
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:32,994
You look like
you're feeling pretty refreshed.

178
00:07:33,077 --> 00:07:34,745
- [giggles]
- Huh? Let's go in.

179
00:07:38,249 --> 00:07:40,168
- [Ruru] Wow, it's warm.
- [Awich laughs]

180
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:42,503
[Megumi]<i> These two look</i>
<i>kind of good together.</i>

181
00:07:47,049 --> 00:07:48,050
[Ruru] This feels good.

182
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:51,429
So at the moment,
what's the lay of the land like?

183
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:54,140
What's the situation?

184
00:07:54,223 --> 00:07:56,559
Assun and Ma-kun.

185
00:07:56,642 --> 00:07:59,270
- I see that, yeah.
- Assun is going for Ma-kun.

186
00:07:59,353 --> 00:08:01,814
I was interested in Leo to begin with.

187
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:03,191
And now?

188
00:08:03,274 --> 00:08:07,487
Well, it's not that I'm not interested,
I just don't know how he feels about me.

189
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:10,573
So, even when
we talk one-on-one, it's like--

190
00:08:10,656 --> 00:08:12,867
- Nothing happens.
- Exactly, nothing happens.

191
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:15,578
- Mmm.
- I don't know how he feels about me.

192
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:17,038
You're not going to make a move?

193
00:08:17,121 --> 00:08:19,582
- I would if I was sure it was love.
- Uh-huh.

194
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:23,503
But, yeah, I think out of all the guys,
he's the only one I like.

195
00:08:23,586 --> 00:08:25,296
- [Kazu-kun] Mmm.
- I'm interested in him.

196
00:08:25,379 --> 00:08:26,255
I think?

197
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:28,799
It's like I'm half interested in him
right now.

198
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:30,593
[laughs] So you're not fully interested.

199
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:33,554
Right. Because, I mean,
he hasn't made a move either.

200
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:36,724
- [Kazu-kun] Hmm.
- So I'm like, "What's going on?"

201
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:37,725
I see.

202
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:43,981
[Megumi and Nagano laugh]

203
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,108
- [Nagano] <i>Drinking away.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Meanwhile, Leo…</i>

204
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:48,986
[Ari] How do you feel right now?

205
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:52,865
- Well, I'm not happy.
- [Bo] Yeah, figures.

206
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:54,158
- [Ma-kun] Yeah.
- Yeah.

207
00:08:55,743 --> 00:08:59,038
People have this image of me
as a notorious player…

208
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:00,623
Uh-huh, yeah.

209
00:09:00,706 --> 00:09:03,960
- …and that image has stuck.
- Yeah. That's the image I have.

210
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:07,338
[laughs] And we've had
a drink together once before.

211
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:09,298
- Yeah, we have.
- Yeah, you remember?

212
00:09:09,382 --> 00:09:11,842
I don't remember where exactly,
but I'm sure you were

213
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:13,678
- in that circle of people.
- Uh-huh, yeah.

214
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:14,929
Yeah, I thought so.

215
00:09:15,513 --> 00:09:17,431
- [Megumi] They've met before.
- You were right.

216
00:09:17,515 --> 00:09:19,141
Her face looked like they'd met before.

217
00:09:19,225 --> 00:09:20,893
- [Nagano] You were saying that.
- Hmm.

218
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:23,813
I was surprised when the door opened.
Like, seriously?

219
00:09:23,896 --> 00:09:26,607
- [chuckles]
- I was like, "They chose him?" [chuckles]

220
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:28,150
- You were on their sign.
- Mm.

221
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:29,485
I already knew who you were.

222
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:31,737
I was telling everyone about this host

223
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:33,447
- who I thought was handsome.
- Oh, wow.

224
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:36,158
- Are you a fortune-teller?
- [Nagano] Right?

225
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:38,619
- You keep guessing--
- Are you cheating?

226
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:41,789
- Have you already seen the footage?
- I'm not cheating. I just…

227
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:44,750
have detective skills.

228
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:46,002
Now you're scaring me.

229
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:48,045
- Another.
- Detective skills?

230
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:49,839
Huh? You know if someone's lying?

231
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:53,134
- I can tell when someone's lying.
- Or you can tell what they're thinking?

232
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:55,428
When it comes to love,
I can tell straight away.

233
00:09:55,511 --> 00:09:56,429
[both] Wow.

234
00:09:56,512 --> 00:09:57,722
- That's reassuring.
- Yeah.

235
00:09:57,805 --> 00:09:59,640
I don't know what Ruru's thinking.

236
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:00,975
Mmm.

237
00:10:01,058 --> 00:10:05,396
I'm starting to wonder if
she's actually even interested in Leo.

238
00:10:05,479 --> 00:10:09,358
Yeah. She said something like
she's only half-interested in him.

239
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:11,902
- Like, is that even a real thing?
- [laughs]

240
00:10:11,986 --> 00:10:13,195
I don't think so.

241
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,823
- I mean, is it really that difficult?
- She's half interested.

242
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:19,493
- [Megumi]<i> It's so intense.</i>
- [Nagano]<i> It's so erotic, like…</i>

243
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:21,829
<i>- It's like watching porn.</i>
- [Megumi laughs]<i> I get that!</i>

244
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:23,164
[Awich]<i> But it looks beautiful.</i>

245
00:10:23,247 --> 00:10:24,707
This is just a little tidbit,

246
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:27,668
but a friend of mine was watching
the last <i>Badly In Love,</i>

247
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:30,963
he was watching on his phone,
and he was so turned on by it,

248
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:34,216
that he tried to pinch in it to zoom,
but you can't do that on Netflix.

249
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,093
- [laughing]
- Yeah. He was frustrated.

250
00:10:36,177 --> 00:10:37,678
That makes me happy, he got sucked in.

251
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:39,263
He kept trying with his finger…

252
00:10:39,347 --> 00:10:41,599
To zoom in on it?
'Cause he was watching on his phone.

253
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:42,725
He wanted to see the body.

254
00:10:42,808 --> 00:10:45,853
- Poor guy, you can't zoom in on Netflix.
- I'm sorry, my--

255
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:47,897
- There are fans who are like my friend.
- [Awich] I see.

256
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:49,815
- [Megumi] Fans of the sauna time.
- Yes.

257
00:10:49,899 --> 00:10:52,985
- [Ha-chan] He has a really handsome face.
- [women laugh]

258
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:55,655
- I thought he was handsome.
- He has a beautiful face.

259
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:56,989
ASSUN (30)
ENTREPRENEUR/HOSTESS

260
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:58,741
Anyone would think he's handsome.

261
00:10:58,824 --> 00:11:01,202
I wanted him to choose me for the sauna.

262
00:11:01,285 --> 00:11:03,162
- [Assun] You did?
- I wanted him to choose me.

263
00:11:03,245 --> 00:11:04,747
[Nagano and Megumi]<i> What?</i>

264
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:05,915
[Awich]<i> She's honest.</i>

265
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:11,629
I'm super curious about what you're like
when you fall for somebody

266
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:14,548
and how you're gonna play things
while you're here at the academy.

267
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:16,967
- [both laugh]
- I can't imagine it at all.

268
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:21,138
I'm all or nothing. If I'm not interested
in someone, then there's nothing there.

269
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:22,890
- Okay, I see.
- Yeah.

270
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:24,850
[Ruru] All or nothing is way better.

271
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:27,895
- [Kazu-kun] Right?
- Yeah, definitely better.

272
00:11:30,439 --> 00:11:32,817
- [Assun] Here she comes.
- [all] Welcome back.

273
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:35,319
- [Assun] How'd it go?
- [Ha-chan] She's got a huge smile.

274
00:11:35,403 --> 00:11:37,947
- [Assun] She looks happy.
- [Ha-chan] What happened?

275
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:40,282
I think I like sauna time now. It was fun.

276
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:42,034
- Oh!
- Oh, really?

277
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:44,286
When I was in there with Ma-kun,

278
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:47,206
it was a little awkward,
but it wasn't awkward this time.

279
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:51,961
I already thought he was good-looking,
so I just told him what I thought.

280
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:53,629
Mmm.

281
00:11:53,712 --> 00:11:56,632
So I told him he's my type
and I think he's good-looking.

282
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:58,676
- [Assun] Yeah.
- That's what happened.

283
00:12:06,183 --> 00:12:08,519
[Megumi]<i> What's he going to do</i>
<i>in the men's room?</i>

284
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:11,856
[Leo] I'm not worried.

285
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,858
- Excuse me.
- [Leo] You know?

286
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,737
Hi, guys. Can we talk?

287
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:22,408
[sighs, grunts]

288
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:25,744
There was a slight misunderstanding

289
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:28,497
when I said I didn't want
to be friends with you guys.

290
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:32,334
And there's no room for romance
when things are awkward like this.

291
00:12:32,918 --> 00:12:36,213
I said it
because I want to find love here.

292
00:12:36,297 --> 00:12:41,552
But if I'm all, like, buddy-buddy,
I have a habit of giving up on the girl

293
00:12:41,635 --> 00:12:44,054
if one of my friends also likes her.

294
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:47,766
So I said it because I didn't want
to get too friendly with you guys.

295
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:50,811
But I, low-key,
do want to get along with you.

296
00:12:52,188 --> 00:12:53,314
What do you say?

297
00:12:53,397 --> 00:12:54,482
- [Ma-kun] Sure.
- Yeah.

298
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:56,525
You just gotta tell us.

299
00:12:57,026 --> 00:12:59,570
- I'm sorry I broke your chain.
- Nah, I'm sorry too.

300
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:01,655
Was the curry good?

301
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:04,074
It was, but I was so full
of adrenaline, I couldn't eat.

302
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:06,535
- Hey, that's exactly what you said.
- I told you, didn't I?

303
00:13:06,619 --> 00:13:09,079
- [Ma-kun] Couldn't taste it, huh?
- [Leo] He said you wouldn't.

304
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:11,707
I was thinking,
"I can't swallow this. Damn it."

305
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:14,877
[Megumi] <i>Bo's also smiling. That's good.</i>

306
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:17,254
- What the…
- They're so adorable.

307
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:18,756
- No, no, wait.
- Huh?

308
00:13:18,839 --> 00:13:21,675
- I'm the only one who's still mad.
- Right? Me too.

309
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:22,635
- Right?
- I'm with you.

310
00:13:22,718 --> 00:13:24,845
- You're still mad?
- I'm mad at Kazu-kun's attitude.

311
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:27,306
- [Megumi] Jeez, you take your time.
- Why'd they forgive him?

312
00:13:27,389 --> 00:13:29,642
You guys were the ones
who stirred it up and made me mad.

313
00:13:29,725 --> 00:13:31,894
He said,
"Thank you for the curry, Ma-kun."

314
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:34,271
- Isn't that enough?
- So that means you can say anything?

315
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:37,024
If you feel that something's off,
you can't move on?

316
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:38,567
Uh, that's right.

317
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:41,654
- You've been with us since Season 1.
- [Nagano] Yes.

318
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:43,697
I'd like you
to not come back to this every time.

319
00:13:43,781 --> 00:13:45,574
- I'd also like that.
- Let's do our best.

320
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,660
I think a lot of viewers
will be feeling the same.

321
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:50,913
Like some middle-aged man
watching <i>Badly In Love</i> really furious.

322
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:51,872
[Megumi] That's true.

323
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:53,040
LOVE DINER

324
00:13:53,123 --> 00:13:56,126
- [Hikaru] Are there more dishes to clean?
- [Bo] Tai-chan brought some.

325
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:57,878
[Leo] Yeah, I don't mind, though.

326
00:13:57,962 --> 00:13:59,505
MARIRIN (25)
BAR WORKER

327
00:14:02,883 --> 00:14:06,804
You know, Bo, I got pushed real hard,
when you beat him up.

328
00:14:08,305 --> 00:14:09,848
- I got pushed really hard.
- Oh, yeah?

329
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:10,766
[Maririn] Yeah.

330
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:13,936
And I was like, "Oh, yeah? Seriously?"

331
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:15,938
[Nagano]<i> "Yeah, seriously"?</i>

332
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:18,941
[Megumi]<i> Well, she found out</i>
<i>that Bo raised his hand to a girl, so…</i>

333
00:14:19,024 --> 00:14:20,025
[Nagano]<i> Oh, I see.</i>

334
00:14:26,657 --> 00:14:28,576
<i>Violence is scary, for sure.</i>

335
00:14:28,659 --> 00:14:29,493
[Megumi]<i> Yeah.</i>

336
00:14:35,499 --> 00:14:36,709
Hey, Maririn.

337
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:41,881
- Hey, thanks for coming.
- [Ma-kun] No problem.

338
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:45,843
So, Maririn was talking to me earlier on,

339
00:14:46,343 --> 00:14:48,053
- and it was about Bo.
- Yeah.

340
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:53,851
I think Maririn's main issue
is trying to overcome her past trauma.

341
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:56,520
That's the biggest thing.
She can't fall in love.

342
00:14:56,604 --> 00:15:00,524
So Bo, Maririn, Ruru, and Leo

343
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,359
were all talking together.

344
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:03,694
- [Maririn] Yeah.
- [Ma-kun] Mmm.

345
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:07,406
And during the conversation, Bo mentioned
that he has hit a woman before.

346
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:09,366
Yeah, he said he hit a woman.

347
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:11,327
What?

348
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:14,079
So that conversation happened,

349
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:16,123
and then you know
how he hit the transfer student?

350
00:15:16,206 --> 00:15:17,541
[Ma-kun] Uh-huh. Yeah.

351
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:19,752
- I got pushed really hard.
- [Ma-kun] Yeah.

352
00:15:19,835 --> 00:15:23,422
And while we were doing the dishes,
I told him I got pushed,

353
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:25,299
and he was like, "Oh, yeah?"

354
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:29,553
And I was like, "Oh, so that's how it is."

355
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:31,472
And I wanted to say something back,

356
00:15:31,555 --> 00:15:34,391
you know, like,
"Aren't you going to apologize?"

357
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:37,603
But I was scared he might hit me.
So I didn't.

358
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:40,064
- Let's talk to him.
- [Maririn] Yeah.

359
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:41,774
- Yeah. I'll get him.
- [Assun] Okay.

360
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:43,692
- [Maririn] Yeah.
- If there's any bad blood, then…

361
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:46,195
- Yeah.
- [Awich]<i> He's showing his strength.</i>

362
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:47,613
[Megumi]<i> That's Ma-kun.</i>

363
00:15:52,284 --> 00:15:54,495
[Ma-kun] Do you remember
what Maririn said?

364
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:57,915
- How she was abused by her ex-boyfriend?
- Yeah.

365
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:58,874
Yeah.

366
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:02,169
[Ma-kun] Girls are scared of that.
Guys are stronger than girls.

367
00:16:02,252 --> 00:16:03,087
Mmm-hmm.

368
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:06,924
[Ma-kun] Right?
And earlier, you slammed into her.

369
00:16:07,007 --> 00:16:07,925
Mmm-hmm.

370
00:16:08,008 --> 00:16:10,928
- When you were fighting with Kazuma.
- Oh, sorry about that.

371
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:16,225
But you didn't apologize earlier.

372
00:16:16,850 --> 00:16:19,645
Oh, sorry about that.
I wasn't considerate enough.

373
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:20,604
- Sorry.
- Yeah.

374
00:16:21,146 --> 00:16:22,106
It's okay.

375
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:25,025
Cheating is definitely not okay.

376
00:16:25,109 --> 00:16:26,193
- Definitely.
- Hmm, yeah.

377
00:16:26,276 --> 00:16:27,361
No matter how you look at it.

378
00:16:27,444 --> 00:16:28,487
But guys…

379
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:30,656
should never hit girls.

380
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:32,658
- Never.
- [Ma-kun] They're not as strong as us.

381
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:34,159
- We shouldn't do it.
- [Ma-kun] Yeah.

382
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:36,286
Do you promise not to hit a woman?

383
00:16:37,204 --> 00:16:38,080
Yeah, I promise.

384
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:40,833
- Thank you for talking to me.
- Now make peace.

385
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:42,042
- I mean--
- Let's make peace.

386
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:45,170
- Wow, you can spread your legs super wide.
- [laughing]

387
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:47,297
- Never seen that.
- [Assun] Your hips are flexible.

388
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,883
[Ma-kun] Bo's such a yankii,
know what I mean?

389
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:51,260
- Sorry.
- [Maririn] No worries.

390
00:16:51,343 --> 00:16:52,511
[Megumi]<i> I'm so glad.</i>

391
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:56,098
[PA system chiming]

392
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:01,270
[boy on PA] <i>So, today's Valentine's Day.</i>

393
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:03,147
- I forgot about it.
- They're telling us.

394
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,899
[boy on PA]<i> A day</i>
<i>for expressing love and gratitude</i>

395
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:08,610
<i>to your partner</i>
<i>or someone important to you.</i>

396
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:13,157
<i>Gentlemen, your task</i>
<i>is to prepare a homemade box of candy</i>

397
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:17,953
<i>to let the woman you're interested in</i>
<i>know exactly how you feel about her.</i>

398
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:20,706
- Task understood.
- [Ma-kun] All right!

399
00:17:20,789 --> 00:17:22,583
- Let's do this! Come on!
- Wassup!

400
00:17:22,666 --> 00:17:23,584
Let's go!

401
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:27,171
[Megumi]<i> What the heck?</i>
<i>They were fighting just a second ago.</i>

402
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:28,338
[Ma-kun] Wow!

403
00:17:28,839 --> 00:17:31,050
[romantic music playing]

404
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:45,064
- [Nagano]<i> He's so dexterous.</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Bo's drawing a heart.</i>

405
00:17:45,564 --> 00:17:47,941
[Ari] This would be better
with white chocolate.

406
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:51,445
I didn't know this was what
giving candy feels like.

407
00:17:53,822 --> 00:17:54,990
TAISEI

408
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,158
SUCH AN ANGEL

409
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:57,951
- [Nagano]<i> Wow. Tai-chan.</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Oh, my.</i>

410
00:17:58,035 --> 00:17:59,161
TAI-CHAN'S CREATION

411
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:01,663
- [Megumi] <i>Their personalities are showing.</i>
- [Nagano]<i> So cute.</i>

412
00:18:01,747 --> 00:18:06,835
MA-KUN'S CREATION

413
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:12,007
KAZU-KUN'S CREATION

414
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:13,300
BO'S CREATION

415
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:14,301
[Nagano]<i> Bo.</i>

416
00:18:14,384 --> 00:18:16,595
- [Awich]<i> Bo's is adorable.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>So lovely.</i>

417
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:18,180
- [Nagano]<i> Cute.</i>
- [Awich]<i> It's badass.</i>

418
00:18:20,849 --> 00:18:22,559
- [Megumi] <i>He's done fruit!</i>
- [Nagano chuckles]

419
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:24,728
- [Megumi]<i> Nice.</i>
- [Nagano]<i> Nice.</i>

420
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:26,563
ARI'S CREATION

421
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:33,195
TO RURU
HAPPY BALEN

422
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:35,739
It's a "T-A." Cross out the "N."

423
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:38,117
- "N-N-T…"?
- "N-N-T-A."

424
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,243
"N"? "Valentine"?

425
00:18:39,326 --> 00:18:40,828
- Yo, you're useless!
- [Ma-kun laughs]

426
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:41,995
Don't bother.

427
00:18:42,079 --> 00:18:43,831
Hey, hold on.
If I'm useless, then so's he.

428
00:18:43,914 --> 00:18:46,125
"Ba-re-."
Like I'm typing on the computer.

429
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:47,835
Bro, you're using romaji!

430
00:18:47,918 --> 00:18:50,879
- Didn't you say romaji?
- That just sounds out the words!

431
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:53,882
- [both laughing]
- Come on, bro! Seriously, what the hell?

432
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:55,884
Like, who the hell would do that?

433
00:18:56,552 --> 00:19:00,097
Why would I write it out in romaji?
Huh? Idiot!

434
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,348
[Awich]<i> They're having fun.</i>

435
00:19:01,431 --> 00:19:03,475
[Leo] I asked for the spelling in English!

436
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:04,935
[laughing]

437
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:06,937
This kind of thing is always the most fun.

438
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:08,522
- Right?
- [Nagano] Yeah.

439
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:11,191
LEO'S CREATION

440
00:19:11,275 --> 00:19:12,276
[Nagano]<i> He's good.</i>

441
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:14,945
- [Awich]<i> Leo's good at this.</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Leo is really good.</i>

442
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:16,947
- [Awich]<i> He might be the best.</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Wow.</i>

443
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:21,076
I think the chocolates Kazuma made
will be really good.

444
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:23,162
You want 'em. [laughs]

445
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:24,454
[Maririn] She does.

446
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:27,875
- I bet Kazuma's will be really good.
- Hmm, Leo's might be better.

447
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:29,042
You think so?

448
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:34,882
[boy on PA] <i>When you have finished,</i>
<i>please go to the office</i>

449
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:38,177
<i>and call the person you like</i>
<i>over the PA system.</i>

450
00:19:42,764 --> 00:19:43,891
[PA system chimes]

451
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:46,393
BROADCASTING

452
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:48,145
It's Ma-kun.

453
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:52,774
My box of candy is for…

454
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:54,860
Assun.

455
00:19:54,943 --> 00:19:55,777
[Nagano]<i> Well, yeah.</i>

456
00:19:56,361 --> 00:19:58,113
[Ma-kun] <i>Please, come to the sauna room.</i>

457
00:19:58,197 --> 00:19:59,364
- The sauna room?
- [Ruru] What?

458
00:20:00,449 --> 00:20:02,034
- Finally! Nice.
- [Ruru] Have fun!

459
00:20:02,117 --> 00:20:04,161
But we're not going to go
in the sauna, are we?

460
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:06,705
[chimes]

461
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:09,833
[man over PA system] <i>One two, one two.</i>

462
00:20:09,917 --> 00:20:11,126
- Who's that?
- Is it Kazuma?

463
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:12,961
- It's Tai-chan.
<i>- Uh, it's Tai-chan.</i>

464
00:20:13,503 --> 00:20:14,880
[Ha-chan chuckling] Oh, no.

465
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:17,466
[Megumi]<i> Who will Tai-chan pick?</i>

466
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:20,427
My box of candy is for…

467
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:26,016
Hikaru.

468
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:29,228
<i>I'll be in the smoking area</i>
<i>in the courtyard.</i>

469
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:31,563
[Assun] He just wanted to smoke,
so he picked there.

470
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:33,857
- [laughs]
- [Nagano]<i> Well, yeah.</i>

471
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:36,151
[Megumi]<i> She looks like</i>
<i>she's really mad at him.</i>

472
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,654
[chimes]

473
00:20:40,864 --> 00:20:42,908
[Bo] <i>My Valentine's Day candy is for…</i>

474
00:20:42,991 --> 00:20:44,701
- [Ruru] That's cute.
- [giggles]

475
00:20:48,997 --> 00:20:49,873
…Hikaru.

476
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:53,585
[Nagano]<i> She's popular.</i>

477
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:55,796
Look at you acting all surprised.

478
00:20:55,879 --> 00:20:58,465
No, I really am.
I didn't know Bo would do that.

479
00:20:59,758 --> 00:21:02,386
[chimes]

480
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:05,973
[Ari] <i>Yo! Mic check,</i>

481
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:07,975
<i>one, two, one, two!</i>

482
00:21:08,058 --> 00:21:10,018
<i>- Wassup!</i>
<i>- </i>[laughing]

483
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:11,979
<i>Uh, it's Ari, uh…</i>

484
00:21:12,604 --> 00:21:15,983
The woman I want to give
my chocolates to is…

485
00:21:18,151 --> 00:21:20,612
<i>Hikaru!</i>

486
00:21:20,696 --> 00:21:22,906
- [Ruru] This is so amazing.
<i>- I want to give them to her…</i>

487
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:25,450
- It's just like, bravo, girl.
<i>- …uh, even though I…</i>

488
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:28,453
I wasn't very good at it.

489
00:21:28,537 --> 00:21:30,330
- I made some chocolates…
- [Ruru] So cute.

490
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,790
…with a lot of love.

491
00:21:31,873 --> 00:21:33,083
[Ruru] So cute.

492
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:35,085
<i>So I'll be waiting in the kitchen.</i>

493
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:37,754
Please come!

494
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:39,506
- That's nice.
- He said it the best.

495
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:40,882
[Kazu-kun] That was nice.

496
00:21:46,388 --> 00:21:47,681
It's Leo here.

497
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,727
<i>I want to give my box of candy…</i>

498
00:21:54,354 --> 00:21:55,564
to Ruru.

499
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:58,025
- [Nagano]<i> Devoted.</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Since day one.</i>

500
00:21:58,108 --> 00:21:59,860
[Leo] <i>I made them with all my love.</i>

501
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:04,489
<i>I'll be waiting behind the gymnasium.</i>
<i>See you there.</i>

502
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:07,242
- [laughing]
- [Hikaru] I think he wants to grill you.

503
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:10,370
He wants to grill you about the fact that
you went to the sauna with Kazuma.

504
00:22:10,454 --> 00:22:12,664
- He's gonna make me <i>dogeza.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>What potty mouths.</i>

505
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:15,459
- [Nagano laughs]
- Hi. It's Kazu-kun.

506
00:22:15,542 --> 00:22:16,835
[Hikaru] It's Kazu-kun.

507
00:22:16,918 --> 00:22:20,213
Uh, I want to give my box of candy…

508
00:22:23,842 --> 00:22:24,760
<i>to Ruru.</i>

509
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:26,136
[Hikaru and Ha-chan] Oh.

510
00:22:28,096 --> 00:22:30,390
- [Hikaru] She's happy.
<i>- Please come to the living room.</i>

511
00:22:30,474 --> 00:22:32,350
- Is it the usual?
- [Hikaru] She's so happy.

512
00:22:32,434 --> 00:22:35,103
- [Ruru] Did he say the living room?
- [Nagano]<i> Oh, no.</i>

513
00:22:36,146 --> 00:22:39,483
Well, well, well. [laughs]

514
00:22:45,489 --> 00:22:46,865
Okay, I'm off.

515
00:22:46,948 --> 00:22:48,533
- [all] Have fun.
- Enjoy.

516
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:51,119
I'll wear Masaya's jacket.

517
00:22:51,203 --> 00:22:52,329
[Ruru] Be careful.

518
00:22:52,412 --> 00:22:53,830
- I'm going.
- [Ruru] See you later.

519
00:22:59,586 --> 00:23:01,963
- Thank you.
- I've never made candy before.

520
00:23:02,047 --> 00:23:05,050
- Yeah, I've never been gifted them either.
- [laughs]

521
00:23:05,133 --> 00:23:06,635
- So you made them?
- I made them.

522
00:23:06,718 --> 00:23:09,221
- It's kind of--
- This is so cute, I love the heart.

523
00:23:09,304 --> 00:23:11,223
- I felt embarrassed making it.
- [both laugh]

524
00:23:11,306 --> 00:23:12,140
Seriously.

525
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:15,769
This is the first time in my life
that I've received a handmade gift.

526
00:23:15,852 --> 00:23:16,812
[laughs]

527
00:23:16,895 --> 00:23:18,563
It's so cute!

528
00:23:19,231 --> 00:23:21,274
<i>- Dang!</i>
- [Ma-kun]<i> I'm glad you like it.</i>

529
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:24,319
[Assun giggles]<i> So did you,</i>
<i>like, decorate it all yourself?</i>

530
00:23:24,402 --> 00:23:26,446
- [Ma-kun]<i> I did.</i>
<i>- </i>[Assun] <i>That's so cute.</i>

531
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:28,156
I thought they'd be the least fattening.

532
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,741
- Strawberries?
- Strawberries.

533
00:23:29,825 --> 00:23:31,201
- Can I eat one?
- Go ahead.

534
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:33,954
- Okay, then. Thank you.
- Mmm.

535
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:36,498
Mmm.

536
00:23:37,457 --> 00:23:38,333
Mmm, it's good.

537
00:23:38,416 --> 00:23:39,668
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

538
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:42,462
They seem comfortable together.

539
00:23:42,546 --> 00:23:43,880
It's a strong bond.

540
00:23:43,964 --> 00:23:45,632
- [Nagano] I know.
- I feel like it is.

541
00:23:45,715 --> 00:23:47,926
- Like an old married couple.
- [both] Yeah.

542
00:23:48,009 --> 00:23:50,220
And they even have a similar tone.

543
00:23:50,303 --> 00:23:52,013
- Look good together.
- [Megumi] They do.

544
00:23:52,097 --> 00:23:56,101
[boy on PA] <i>You are now going to accept</i>
<i>the men's offers of love.</i>

545
00:23:56,184 --> 00:24:00,313
<i>For the ones who received multiple offers</i>
<i>from different men,</i>

546
00:24:00,397 --> 00:24:02,482
<i>you will accept the offers</i>

547
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:05,735
<i>in the order corresponding</i>
<i>to your own feelings.</i>

548
00:24:05,819 --> 00:24:07,154
I can't decide.

549
00:24:07,237 --> 00:24:09,072
- [Ha-chan] You can't?
- [Hikaru] Right?

550
00:24:09,739 --> 00:24:12,200
[pensive music playing]

551
00:24:16,163 --> 00:24:17,873
Which order are you going in?

552
00:24:20,083 --> 00:24:21,459
Oh, what should I do?

553
00:24:21,543 --> 00:24:25,130
[Megumi]<i> That's a luxury problem.</i>
<i>You don't usually get this kind of choice.</i>

554
00:24:31,094 --> 00:24:33,096
- I'm going.
- [Ruru] Hope it goes well.

555
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:34,556
- [Ha-chan] Bye.
- [Ruru] See you.

556
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:40,937
Maybe I'll try being
a little more aggressive.

557
00:24:41,605 --> 00:24:43,815
- I can't go on like this.
- Yeah.

558
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,741
[Megumi]<i> Who will Hikaru go to first?</i>

559
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:57,329
[gasps softly]

560
00:25:07,505 --> 00:25:08,757
- [Awich]<i> Huh?</i>
- [Nagano]<i> What?</i>

561
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:12,177
[Megumi]<i> She just walked straight past him</i>
<i>and went somewhere else.</i>

562
00:25:19,059 --> 00:25:21,770
- Wassup, man?
- Wassup, man?

563
00:25:21,853 --> 00:25:23,396
[chuckles] Wassup, man?

564
00:25:24,272 --> 00:25:26,024
- [Nagano]<i> Well, that's unexpected.</i>
- Hey.

565
00:25:27,025 --> 00:25:28,568
- Have a seat.
- [exhales]

566
00:25:28,652 --> 00:25:30,487
- Hey. Am I the first?
- Mmm-hmm.

567
00:25:30,987 --> 00:25:32,697
Oh, I see.

568
00:25:33,490 --> 00:25:34,324
I made this.

569
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:36,993
- Thank you.
- Yes, to Hikaru.

570
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:38,411
I made this for you.

571
00:25:38,495 --> 00:25:42,666
I thought you might be on a diet,
so I made sure it was mostly fruit.

572
00:25:42,749 --> 00:25:45,460
- Oh, really?
- I thought you might not want chocolate.

573
00:25:45,543 --> 00:25:49,005
So I thought that if it was all
just chocolate, it might be too much.

574
00:25:49,089 --> 00:25:50,799
Why am I the first?

575
00:25:50,882 --> 00:25:52,133
I thought about it a lot,

576
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:55,053
and out of everybody
who's been expressing their feelings…

577
00:25:55,136 --> 00:25:55,971
Yeah.

578
00:25:56,054 --> 00:25:58,807
…you've been
expressing your feelings to me the most.

579
00:26:00,058 --> 00:26:02,227
Wow! You're a genius.

580
00:26:02,310 --> 00:26:03,311
- [Ari] Right?
- Yeah.

581
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:05,647
[Ari] Wasn't sure if you'd like it
'cause it's chocolate.

582
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:07,107
[Hikaru] It's really good.

583
00:26:08,191 --> 00:26:10,026
- Yum!
- Is it good? You like it?

584
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:11,569
Here.

585
00:26:18,326 --> 00:26:19,786
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

586
00:26:19,869 --> 00:26:21,621
I'm so happy you came to me first.

587
00:26:22,914 --> 00:26:23,748
Here you go.

588
00:26:24,249 --> 00:26:25,834
- Thank you.
- Let's shake hands.

589
00:26:27,252 --> 00:26:29,045
- Wassup, man?
- Yeah, I feel you.

590
00:26:29,129 --> 00:26:30,338
[Nagano]<i> I like his honesty.</i>

591
00:26:30,422 --> 00:26:32,382
- [Awich]<i> Yeah.</i>
- [Nagano]<i> He says what he thinks.</i>

592
00:26:32,465 --> 00:26:33,591
[Megumi]<i> Adorable.</i>

593
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:38,972
- [Nagano laughs]<i> That's so adorable.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Aw, that's cute.</i>

594
00:26:39,055 --> 00:26:40,932
- So cute!
- [Nagano] <i>Like in </i>Platoon.

595
00:26:42,809 --> 00:26:45,145
- Awesome!
- [Nagano laughs]

596
00:26:45,228 --> 00:26:49,149
I've never seen anyone do that except
for when they score a goal in soccer.

597
00:26:49,232 --> 00:26:51,276
- Now you have.
- It looks exactly like that.

598
00:26:58,033 --> 00:27:02,078
- [Hikaru] Sorry to keep you waiting.
- [Tai-chan] Happy Valentine's Day.

599
00:27:02,162 --> 00:27:03,955
Happy Valentine's Day.

600
00:27:04,539 --> 00:27:07,584
I've never done this before,
but I'd like to give you some candy.

601
00:27:07,667 --> 00:27:10,003
Thank you. [gasps] What a cute bag.

602
00:27:10,086 --> 00:27:11,629
I'm glad you like it.

603
00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:14,257
I realized when I made it
that you won't be able to eat it all.

604
00:27:14,341 --> 00:27:15,800
- Why not?
- There's a lot in there.

605
00:27:16,676 --> 00:27:18,553
Huh? Oh my god, wait.

606
00:27:18,636 --> 00:27:20,263
- This is so cute!
- You can take it out.

607
00:27:23,266 --> 00:27:25,310
- You have crazy good taste.
- Right?

608
00:27:25,852 --> 00:27:27,604
I've got good taste in everything.

609
00:27:28,229 --> 00:27:30,148
It's so cute! I want to display it.

610
00:27:30,231 --> 00:27:31,107
- Really?
- Yeah.

611
00:27:31,816 --> 00:27:34,319
- You've really changed for real.
- What do you mean?

612
00:27:34,402 --> 00:27:37,197
- I mean, I can tell.
- Which means?

613
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:40,033
At first, I thought you were such a sissy.

614
00:27:40,116 --> 00:27:40,992
[Tai-chan] Mmm.

615
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:44,496
But now when I see you talking
to all of the other guys in here,

616
00:27:44,579 --> 00:27:48,375
like, I think,
"Oh, he's definitely a guy."

617
00:27:48,458 --> 00:27:49,959
- You think that, do you?
- Yeah.

618
00:27:50,043 --> 00:27:52,712
- For real? Well, I'm glad you can tell.
- Mmm-hmm.

619
00:27:52,796 --> 00:27:53,671
Good night then.

620
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:55,382
- Good night. Thanks.
- I feel better.

621
00:27:55,465 --> 00:27:57,258
- [Hikaru] Thank you. Thank you.
- Good night.

622
00:27:59,552 --> 00:28:00,428
Cute.

623
00:28:02,430 --> 00:28:05,141
I can't confess my feelings yet, can I?

624
00:28:06,851 --> 00:28:08,186
- [Bo] Here.
- [Hikaru] Thank you.

625
00:28:08,269 --> 00:28:09,104
Yeah.

626
00:28:11,981 --> 00:28:13,233
Oh, here you go.

627
00:28:14,025 --> 00:28:16,152
- Thank you.
- It's not the best, but…

628
00:28:17,237 --> 00:28:18,279
Oh! That's cute.

629
00:28:18,363 --> 00:28:19,697
I never would have thought

630
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:22,450
that you'd make something
like this, Bo, like, seriously.

631
00:28:23,201 --> 00:28:24,327
It's cute.

632
00:28:24,411 --> 00:28:25,954
You've taken me by surprise.

633
00:28:26,663 --> 00:28:27,831
- Huh?
- By surprise.

634
00:28:27,914 --> 00:28:28,873
[both chuckle]

635
00:28:28,957 --> 00:28:32,669
I guess that the girl
who I like the most is you, Hikaru.

636
00:28:34,087 --> 00:28:35,046
- Mmm.
- Yeah.

637
00:28:36,548 --> 00:28:39,884
- The order was Ari, Tai, then Bo.
- Hmm. Mmm.

638
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:42,429
And that's because

639
00:28:43,304 --> 00:28:45,682
you're still the one
I know the least about.

640
00:28:45,765 --> 00:28:47,892
- That's true. You don't really know much.
- Let's talk.

641
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:49,060
To be honest,

642
00:28:49,144 --> 00:28:52,439
when I heard that you had
raised a hand to a girl before,

643
00:28:53,106 --> 00:28:54,065
I was like, "What?!"

644
00:28:54,149 --> 00:28:55,066
Mmm.

645
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:57,110
- Like, "Bou, really?"
- Mmm.

646
00:28:57,944 --> 00:29:00,363
I wanted people to know about me.

647
00:29:00,864 --> 00:29:04,075
And so I talked about it, even though
I thought it would be negative.

648
00:29:04,159 --> 00:29:05,952
- Mmm.
- The negative part of me.

649
00:29:06,035 --> 00:29:08,037
- That's also part of who I am.
- Mmm.

650
00:29:08,121 --> 00:29:10,999
And because I told them,
I now see things differently.

651
00:29:11,082 --> 00:29:14,002
- Mmm.
- Now, I really strongly believe that

652
00:29:14,085 --> 00:29:17,130
- I should never hit a girl ever again.
- Mmm.

653
00:29:17,630 --> 00:29:18,715
It was bad that I hit her,

654
00:29:18,798 --> 00:29:22,051
but I see things differently now
because of that experience.

655
00:29:22,135 --> 00:29:23,011
Mmm.

656
00:29:24,220 --> 00:29:25,472
Yeah. That's how it is.

657
00:29:29,726 --> 00:29:31,686
- I'm going!
- [Maririn] Bye.

658
00:29:33,855 --> 00:29:34,898
[Megumi]<i> Ruru…</i>

659
00:29:38,193 --> 00:29:40,779
How can she be so happy
in front of these two?

660
00:29:40,862 --> 00:29:43,865
- [laughs] Yeah, I know.
- Yeah, you're absolutely right.

661
00:29:43,948 --> 00:29:45,408
- That's true.
- That's what's amazing.

662
00:29:45,492 --> 00:29:46,785
- [Awich] It really is.
- About Ruru.

663
00:30:01,466 --> 00:30:03,176
[Nagano] <i>Which one will she go to?</i>

664
00:30:05,220 --> 00:30:07,180
- Hey. [giggles]
- [Nagano]<i> What?</i>

665
00:30:07,263 --> 00:30:08,515
- Hey.
- [Ruru] Hey.

666
00:30:09,641 --> 00:30:12,393
- This is for you.
- Thank you! Yay!

667
00:30:12,936 --> 00:30:14,145
What? This is so cute.

668
00:30:14,229 --> 00:30:16,022
This is the first time
I've ever made candy.

669
00:30:16,105 --> 00:30:17,106
- [laughs]
- For real.

670
00:30:17,190 --> 00:30:18,733
Oh, it's so cute!

671
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:20,318
- You're good at it.
- No way.

672
00:30:20,401 --> 00:30:21,778
[Ruru] It's so cute.

673
00:30:23,530 --> 00:30:25,323
Mmm! It's good.

674
00:30:25,406 --> 00:30:26,407
Marshmallow?

675
00:30:26,491 --> 00:30:28,827
- Yeah, I think so.
- Mmm! It's good.

676
00:30:30,912 --> 00:30:33,581
I thought there was a chance
you wouldn't come to me first.

677
00:30:33,665 --> 00:30:35,041
- Mmm.
- It's my first day.

678
00:30:35,124 --> 00:30:37,085
I was like, "Damn" and then, "Oh, well,

679
00:30:37,168 --> 00:30:39,295
it can't be helped,
but it's pretty tough."

680
00:30:39,379 --> 00:30:40,213
- Right.
- Yeah.

681
00:30:40,296 --> 00:30:42,340
- I'm glad I was first.
- Yeah?

682
00:30:45,718 --> 00:30:46,678
[sighs]

683
00:30:48,096 --> 00:30:49,806
[Megumi]<i> Oh, Leo.</i>

684
00:30:55,979 --> 00:30:57,480
Well, this is nice.

685
00:30:58,481 --> 00:30:59,649
What are you giving me?

686
00:31:00,149 --> 00:31:03,695
Well, I'd like us to spend
more time talking together.

687
00:31:06,322 --> 00:31:07,532
- Let's talk.
- Let's talk.

688
00:31:08,283 --> 00:31:10,076
- Yeah.
- So stay near me then.

689
00:31:10,159 --> 00:31:11,536
- [Nagano]<i> Oh.</i>
- Take action.

690
00:31:11,619 --> 00:31:12,579
- [Megumi]<i> Oh, my.</i>
- Okay.

691
00:31:12,662 --> 00:31:15,081
- Then we'll be able to talk a lot.
- True.

692
00:31:24,132 --> 00:31:25,216
- [Ruru] Hey!
- Hey.

693
00:31:25,300 --> 00:31:27,468
- [giggles] Aren't you cold?
- I am.

694
00:31:27,552 --> 00:31:29,095
- It's cold!
- You've already got one.

695
00:31:29,178 --> 00:31:32,098
I intentionally saved you for last
'cause I wanted to talk.

696
00:31:32,181 --> 00:31:33,892
- Really?
- Yeah. I did it on purpose.

697
00:31:33,975 --> 00:31:35,894
- Ooh-ooh!
- Hello!

698
00:31:35,977 --> 00:31:37,270
Wow, this girl.

699
00:31:37,353 --> 00:31:38,730
- [Nagano] Scary.
- [Megumi] "This girl."

700
00:31:38,813 --> 00:31:40,690
- Ruru, Awich is angry.
- [Nagano] Detective!

701
00:31:40,773 --> 00:31:41,733
- [Ruru chuckles]
- For real?

702
00:31:41,816 --> 00:31:43,526
- For real, yeah.
- Oh, okay.

703
00:31:43,610 --> 00:31:46,029
I had a short and simple conversation
with him.

704
00:31:46,112 --> 00:31:50,158
But I wanted to talk to you properly, so…
I wanted to yesterday, but we couldn't.

705
00:31:50,241 --> 00:31:53,369
I wanted to spend more time with you,
so I saved you for last.

706
00:31:53,453 --> 00:31:54,370
- Really?
- Yeah.

707
00:31:55,663 --> 00:31:56,831
Thank you for waiting.

708
00:31:58,499 --> 00:32:01,419
- [Ruru] Oh my god. That's amazing!
- I made it with love.

709
00:32:01,502 --> 00:32:04,547
- Please accept it.
- Thank you. Wow, amazing!

710
00:32:04,631 --> 00:32:07,216
Wow, it's so… wow! It's so cute!

711
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:09,135
- [Leo] I wanted to make a toy poodle.
- I see.

712
00:32:09,218 --> 00:32:12,263
[Leo] But I just couldn't picture
a toy poodle in my head.

713
00:32:12,347 --> 00:32:13,890
[Ruru laughs] I'll eat it later.

714
00:32:13,973 --> 00:32:15,058
- [Leo] Okay.
- In our room.

715
00:32:15,141 --> 00:32:18,686
I mean, you and I
do spend a lot of time together,

716
00:32:18,770 --> 00:32:20,730
but we haven't really
talked about our feelings.

717
00:32:20,813 --> 00:32:22,357
I was thinking the same thing.

718
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:26,277
That's why I've been thinking I want
to tell you that I feel like I have to…

719
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:28,404
- just say it.
- Or we can't move forward.

720
00:32:28,488 --> 00:32:30,531
- Exactly.
- Yeah, I've been thinking the same thing.

721
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,951
- So the way I feel about you is…
- Yeah?

722
00:32:33,034 --> 00:32:34,494
I'm interested in you.

723
00:32:36,955 --> 00:32:39,040
And I know you're also interested in me,

724
00:32:39,123 --> 00:32:42,293
but you're not, like,
expressing it or putting it into words.

725
00:32:42,377 --> 00:32:45,588
So, for me, it's like,
what are you actually thinking?

726
00:32:47,799 --> 00:32:48,758
To be honest…

727
00:32:51,260 --> 00:32:55,014
whether it's the dates, the meals,
or the one-on-ones,

728
00:32:55,932 --> 00:32:57,266
I'd only choose you, Ruru.

729
00:32:58,935 --> 00:33:00,478
- Uh-huh.
- Yeah.

730
00:33:01,229 --> 00:33:02,063
And…

731
00:33:02,730 --> 00:33:06,651
I want to be with you all the time.
Like, when I saw the transfer student,

732
00:33:06,734 --> 00:33:08,444
- Kazu, sitting next to you…
- Yeah?

733
00:33:08,528 --> 00:33:11,531
[Leo] …I was like,
"What the hell is this guy doing?"

734
00:33:11,614 --> 00:33:12,740
[Ruru] Mmm.

735
00:33:12,824 --> 00:33:16,202
I want to date somebody
who I can think about the future with.

736
00:33:17,036 --> 00:33:19,414
- You're mainly in Kyoto, right?
- Mmm-hmm.

737
00:33:19,497 --> 00:33:23,418
And I'm in Tokyo.
So we're both working in different places.

738
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:26,087
- So we'd be long-distance.
- Yeah.

739
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:29,716
- Tokyo, here I come.
- [laughs] That's my main concern.

740
00:33:29,799 --> 00:33:32,510
- We'll cross that bridge later on.
- Yeah, you're right.

741
00:33:33,302 --> 00:33:34,929
I really like you right now.

742
00:33:35,013 --> 00:33:36,973
[romantic music playing]

743
00:33:39,392 --> 00:33:42,103
I don't know what to say,
I just know that I like you.

744
00:33:42,186 --> 00:33:45,898
[laughing] But I genuinely believe
your honesty, Leo.

745
00:33:46,566 --> 00:33:47,525
Thank you.

746
00:33:48,192 --> 00:33:49,694
- See you tomorrow.
- [Leo] Good night.

747
00:33:49,777 --> 00:33:52,155
- [Nagano and Megumi] <i>Aw.</i>
- Good night. Thank you.

748
00:33:57,702 --> 00:33:59,537
Guess I'm moving to Tokyo.

749
00:33:59,620 --> 00:34:01,080
[Awich]<i> Leo is adorable.</i>

750
00:34:02,165 --> 00:34:05,251
Okay, wait, so what
do you guys think about Ruru?

751
00:34:05,334 --> 00:34:06,836
Detective, what do you think?

752
00:34:06,919 --> 00:34:08,755
[inhales sharply] Stay away from her.

753
00:34:09,255 --> 00:34:11,466
[laughs] Yeah,
that's what you wanted to say.

754
00:34:11,549 --> 00:34:14,302
- [Megumi] I mean, to put it simply, yeah.
- So you say, "Stay away from her."

755
00:34:14,385 --> 00:34:18,723
Kazu-kun and Ruru, they're a good match,
in a way, you know?

756
00:34:18,806 --> 00:34:21,601
- Uh-huh, 'cause Kazu-kun is popular.
- [Nagano] Popular.

757
00:34:21,684 --> 00:34:24,937
- I mean, both of them…
- They flirt with each other.

758
00:34:25,021 --> 00:34:26,355
- Yeah, kind of.
- I see.

759
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:30,026
It's like Kazu-kun and Ruru
are playing cards with words.

760
00:34:30,109 --> 00:34:33,112
"This is the first time
I've ever made candy for a girl."

761
00:34:33,196 --> 00:34:35,406
"I want to be with you,
so stay close to me."

762
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:37,408
I mean, they're exchanging techniques.

763
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:39,035
- For sure.
- It's like a duel.

764
00:34:39,118 --> 00:34:41,079
Nothing but techniques,
rather than real words.

765
00:34:41,162 --> 00:34:41,996
[Megumi] Yeah.

766
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:43,790
She's probably
not thinking too much about it,

767
00:34:43,873 --> 00:34:45,124
she's just following her instincts.

768
00:34:45,208 --> 00:34:46,876
"I want to have romance with this person."

769
00:34:46,959 --> 00:34:50,630
"But with this person,
I want to be serious and find out more."

770
00:34:50,713 --> 00:34:53,883
- Yeah, like thinking about the future.
- Maybe that's what she's thinking.

771
00:34:53,966 --> 00:34:57,011
Because she didn't say anything
about the future to Kazu-kun.

772
00:34:57,095 --> 00:34:57,929
[Nagano] She didn't.

773
00:34:58,012 --> 00:35:00,556
But then again, it could also just be that

774
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:04,852
she's keeping Leo as a backup
in case Kazu-kun turns her down.

775
00:35:04,936 --> 00:35:07,772
- [Nagano] Oh, you think so?
- It could be a simple strategy like that.

776
00:35:07,855 --> 00:35:10,274
- Huh. Gosh.
- Oh, look, I don't know anymore.

777
00:35:10,358 --> 00:35:13,069
It seems us three
are the ones getting played by Ruru.

778
00:35:13,152 --> 00:35:15,196
It's like we're trying to read
the mind of a criminal.

779
00:35:15,279 --> 00:35:18,241
This whole time,
we've been treating Ruru like a criminal.

780
00:35:18,324 --> 00:35:20,118
- [both laughing]
- For some reason.

781
00:35:21,077 --> 00:35:23,621
- [thudding]
- [indistinct chatter]

782
00:35:26,249 --> 00:35:28,084
- [Ma-kun] Rock or paper.
- [both] Okay.

783
00:35:28,167 --> 00:35:31,003
- [Nagano]<i> This is…</i>
- [Megumi]<i> A hundred percent tattooed.</i>

784
00:35:31,087 --> 00:35:32,046
[Awich laughs]

785
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:33,714
[Nagano]<i> It looks like</i>
<i>a prison lunch break.</i>

786
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,299
- [Megumi laughs]
- [Awich]<i> So cool.</i>

787
00:35:37,718 --> 00:35:39,011
[Ma-kun whoops]

788
00:35:39,095 --> 00:35:41,097
[both yell]

789
00:35:41,180 --> 00:35:43,182
[rap music playing]

790
00:35:46,435 --> 00:35:48,354
[laughter]

791
00:35:48,437 --> 00:35:50,231
[Ruru] Hey, stop it. For real.

792
00:35:50,314 --> 00:35:51,858
Don't make me laugh.

793
00:35:54,402 --> 00:35:56,362
Wait, mine's the green one, isn't it?

794
00:35:59,991 --> 00:36:01,492
- [Assun] Let's go in.
- [Leo] Good morning.

795
00:36:01,576 --> 00:36:02,660
[Ari] Good morning.

796
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:05,371
I see that you're wearing all black today.

797
00:36:06,372 --> 00:36:08,124
But to me you're pure white,
'cause you're--

798
00:36:08,207 --> 00:36:09,417
- Morning.
- Morning.

799
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:10,543
[laughs]

800
00:36:10,626 --> 00:36:12,879
[Megumi]<i> Guys who say things like that</i>
<i>are adorable.</i>

801
00:36:12,962 --> 00:36:15,131
- [PA system chiming]
- [Ha-chan] Here we go.

802
00:36:18,551 --> 00:36:21,721
[boy on PA] <i>Today,</i>
<i>somebody will get to go on a date.</i>

803
00:36:21,804 --> 00:36:23,556
- [Ma-kun] Yes!
- [Tai-chan] All right!

804
00:36:24,557 --> 00:36:26,475
The guys are
going to have to battle it out.

805
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:28,102
[boy on PA] <i>And that somebody</i>

806
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:32,106
<i>is the person who received</i>
<i>the most Valentine's Day candy.</i>

807
00:36:33,608 --> 00:36:34,609
<i>Hikaru.</i>

808
00:36:35,484 --> 00:36:36,944
- [Leo] Ooh.
- Aw, that sucks.

809
00:36:37,028 --> 00:36:39,822
- I would've won if I got two more.
- [laughter]

810
00:36:39,906 --> 00:36:42,283
[boy on PA] <i>Hikaru,</i>
<i>you are going on a date</i>

811
00:36:42,366 --> 00:36:45,620
<i>with all of the guys</i>
<i>who gave you a box of candy.</i>

812
00:36:45,703 --> 00:36:47,163
- [Assun] All of them?
- Really?

813
00:36:47,246 --> 00:36:49,540
- [Kazu-kun] All of them?
- Huh? Say what?

814
00:36:49,624 --> 00:36:51,876
- You're going with all three.
- [Ha-chan] That's nice.

815
00:36:51,959 --> 00:36:53,502
- Wow, okay.
- [Leo] Uh-huh.

816
00:36:53,586 --> 00:36:55,630
- [Tai-chan] All four of us?
- [Assun] A reverse harem.

817
00:36:57,131 --> 00:36:58,925
[Megumi and Nagano]
This is gonna be tough.

818
00:36:59,008 --> 00:37:00,760
- [Megumi] Gonna be hell.
- How'll she handle this?

819
00:37:00,843 --> 00:37:03,387
They're going to find out
how she acts around their rivals.

820
00:37:03,471 --> 00:37:04,722
- [Nagano] She'll be exposed.
- Yeah.

821
00:37:05,556 --> 00:37:07,808
- Wow, what is this place?
- It's Ryukyu Mura.

822
00:37:07,892 --> 00:37:10,603
Ryukyu! Ryukyu. Wassup<i> shisa!</i>

823
00:37:10,686 --> 00:37:11,646
RYUKYU VILLAGE

824
00:37:14,982 --> 00:37:16,734
- This is so Okinawa.
- This is crazy.

825
00:37:16,817 --> 00:37:17,860
- Oh, wow.
- [Nagano]<i> Don't run.</i>

826
00:37:17,944 --> 00:37:20,655
- [Megumi]<i> They're like kids.</i>
- [Nagano]<i> Shouldn't run in those clothes.</i>

827
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:22,114
- [yelps]
- You okay?

828
00:37:22,198 --> 00:37:23,658
Yeah. My foot nearly slipped.

829
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:25,910
Careful. Careful.

830
00:37:27,286 --> 00:37:29,580
[Ari] There's something
for four people here.

831
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:31,707
[Tai-chan] We drawing a <i>shisa?</i> Okay.

832
00:37:31,791 --> 00:37:34,085
- [Hikaru] Oh! These?
- [Tai-chan] This is what we're painting?

833
00:37:34,168 --> 00:37:37,588
- Looks like we're painting them.
- [Hikaru] Okay, let's decorate the <i>shisa.</i>

834
00:37:37,672 --> 00:37:41,300
If you look at them front on,
the one on the right is the male.

835
00:37:41,801 --> 00:37:44,553
And the female is on the left,
they're a pair.

836
00:37:45,179 --> 00:37:47,890
Why don't we choose
who paints the <i>shisa</i> out of us.

837
00:37:47,974 --> 00:37:49,600
- Hikaru decides.
- Okay.

838
00:37:49,684 --> 00:37:51,310
- [Tai-chan] Go with your gut.
- Okay.

839
00:37:51,394 --> 00:37:54,021
[pleasant music playing]

840
00:38:04,949 --> 00:38:07,493
[laughs] That's your personality
showing through, right?

841
00:38:07,576 --> 00:38:09,870
- That's my personality all over.
- [Hikaru] That's awesome.

842
00:38:09,954 --> 00:38:11,664
- [Ari] Better than Picasso.
- [Hikaru laughs]

843
00:38:11,747 --> 00:38:12,581
[Ari] Isn't it cool?

844
00:38:13,082 --> 00:38:15,334
- [Tai-chan] The theme is anger.
- [Nagano]<i> Awesome.</i>

845
00:38:15,418 --> 00:38:17,253
[Megumi]<i> Tai-chan's so good</i>
<i>with his hands.</i>

846
00:38:17,336 --> 00:38:20,089
[Ari] The theme is
"my feelings for Hikaru."

847
00:38:20,589 --> 00:38:22,591
- I put them into colors.
- [Hikaru] So it's random?

848
00:38:22,675 --> 00:38:24,427
[Ari] It's not random. [laughs]

849
00:38:24,510 --> 00:38:26,846
- [Bo] They're my favorite colors.
- [Tai-chan] Oh, I see.

850
00:38:26,929 --> 00:38:29,015
- [Awich]<i> What a craftsman.</i>
- [Tai-chan] Yellow and green.

851
00:38:29,598 --> 00:38:32,101
- That's the work of a 60-year-old man.
- [laughing]

852
00:38:32,184 --> 00:38:34,770
Really. I mean,
it's like the work of somebody

853
00:38:34,854 --> 00:38:37,356
who's just found out
about the art of subtraction.

854
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:39,984
It's like, "In the end,
it's better not to paint."

855
00:38:40,067 --> 00:38:43,112
Yeah, it's like…
It's like his 10,000th piece of work.

856
00:38:43,195 --> 00:38:45,197
- Yeah, his 10,000th <i>shisa!</i>
- [laughing]

857
00:38:45,281 --> 00:38:47,199
The title is so profound too,
"My Favorite Colors".

858
00:38:47,283 --> 00:38:48,284
- That's true.
- Exactly.

859
00:38:48,868 --> 00:38:52,330
[Nagano]<i> "My Favorite Colors" makes you</i>
<i>wonder about so many different things.</i>

860
00:38:52,413 --> 00:38:55,666
- "My Favorite Colors." [laughing]
- [Nagano] This is too much subtraction.

861
00:38:55,750 --> 00:38:58,044
[Tai-chan] Which one do you feel
has the best set of aesthetics?

862
00:38:58,127 --> 00:39:00,921
- [Bo] This one.
- The one I thought was the cutest was…

863
00:39:02,506 --> 00:39:03,382
Tai-chan's.

864
00:39:03,466 --> 00:39:06,093
Why, thank you. Thank you.

865
00:39:06,177 --> 00:39:09,263
But, hey, there's no, like,
deeper meaning to it.

866
00:39:09,847 --> 00:39:12,600
- Aesthetically, it's Tai-chan's.
- Can I smash this up?

867
00:39:13,184 --> 00:39:14,518
It's pissing me off.

868
00:39:14,602 --> 00:39:15,978
- [Hikaru chuckles]
- [Ari] Just kidding.

869
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:22,735
[boy on PA]<i> There is a nearby banana farm,</i>
<i>which is in need of some young helpers.</i>

870
00:39:22,818 --> 00:39:27,073
<i>The remaining members, please go</i>
<i>down to the banana farm to help out.</i>

871
00:39:27,656 --> 00:39:29,033
- Good morning.
- How are you?

872
00:39:29,116 --> 00:39:30,409
- [Assun] Hello.
- [Leo] Hello.

873
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:31,327
MR. HENTONA

874
00:39:31,410 --> 00:39:32,745
- Yes, welcome.
- Hello, sir.

875
00:39:32,828 --> 00:39:33,913
[Hentona chuckles]

876
00:39:33,996 --> 00:39:36,082
- [Kazu-kun] He's like the final boss.
- [all laugh]

877
00:39:36,165 --> 00:39:37,583
[Ha-chan] Like <i>Dragon Quest.</i>

878
00:39:37,666 --> 00:39:39,418
[Hentona] You all have such good faces.

879
00:39:39,502 --> 00:39:41,128
Nice to meet you. You're strong.

880
00:39:41,212 --> 00:39:43,464
- I can give the guys a hug.
- [Maririn] Aw.

881
00:39:45,424 --> 00:39:47,301
So you'll be sure to come back again.

882
00:39:47,385 --> 00:39:48,594
- Yes, sir.
- Who's the leader?

883
00:39:48,677 --> 00:39:49,762
- Go ahead.
- I am.

884
00:39:49,845 --> 00:39:50,888
Here you are.

885
00:39:50,971 --> 00:39:52,640
- [Leo] Mr. Hentona.
- Yes.

886
00:39:52,723 --> 00:39:54,892
"Mr. Hentona is known for…"

887
00:39:55,768 --> 00:39:56,977
- What's that?
<i>- Bashofu.</i>

888
00:39:57,061 --> 00:39:59,897
…"transforming a village
which was once the home of <i>bashofu,"</i>

889
00:39:59,980 --> 00:40:01,023
"Ogimi village."

890
00:40:01,107 --> 00:40:01,982
- [Assun] Damn.
- Hmm?

891
00:40:02,066 --> 00:40:04,151
- Why don't you read?
- Get him to read it.

892
00:40:04,235 --> 00:40:05,069
You read.

893
00:40:05,152 --> 00:40:07,655
"He is a man
who has dedicated his life to bananas,

894
00:40:07,738 --> 00:40:10,366
transforming Ogimi
back to the home of bananas."

895
00:40:10,449 --> 00:40:11,534
[Assun] Wow.

896
00:40:12,243 --> 00:40:17,498
[boy on PA] <i>He spent ten years creating</i>
<i>an entire banana farm all by himself.</i>

897
00:40:17,581 --> 00:40:18,791
[Nagano]<i> That's amazing.</i>

898
00:40:18,874 --> 00:40:22,294
[boy on PA] <i>Please make sure you work hard</i>
<i>for Mr. Hentona today.</i>

899
00:40:22,378 --> 00:40:24,004
[relaxing music playing]

900
00:40:24,088 --> 00:40:27,800
This is a high-class banana.
They're so good you can eat the skin.

901
00:40:27,883 --> 00:40:29,802
- That's what we have here.
- [Ruru] Wow.

902
00:40:29,885 --> 00:40:31,512
- [Ma-kun] Whoa!
- [Ruru] You can eat the skin?

903
00:40:31,595 --> 00:40:32,972
Wow. Let's go.

904
00:40:34,265 --> 00:40:35,975
- [Hentona] Remove these.
- [Ha-chan] Dead ones?

905
00:40:36,058 --> 00:40:37,309
[Hentona] Remove the dead leaves.

906
00:40:45,901 --> 00:40:49,238
[Ruru] Mr. Hentona, how did you create
this field of banana trees?

907
00:40:50,072 --> 00:40:52,700
- At first, it was a forest like that.
- [Ruru] Really?

908
00:40:52,783 --> 00:40:54,285
It was a really dense forest.

909
00:40:55,077 --> 00:40:58,038
And I used a power shovel
to knock down the trees.

910
00:40:58,122 --> 00:41:00,291
- Uh-huh.
- And then I mowed the grass.

911
00:41:00,374 --> 00:41:01,750
- [Ruru] By yourself?
- By myself.

912
00:41:01,834 --> 00:41:03,335
- [Ruru] Just you?
- Just me.

913
00:41:04,003 --> 00:41:05,212
- [Ruru] Just you?
- Just me.

914
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:07,339
- [Maririn] That's crazy.
- [Ruru] That's insane!

915
00:41:07,423 --> 00:41:08,841
[Hentona] 3.2 acres, four locations.

916
00:41:08,924 --> 00:41:11,218
- [Ruru] All by yourself, right?
- [Hentona] By myself.

917
00:41:11,302 --> 00:41:14,972
- And you work on 5,000 trees by yourself?
- [Hentona] I do it every day.

918
00:41:15,556 --> 00:41:18,100
- What? Do you sleep? Do you sleep?
- [Hentona] Huh? I sleep.

919
00:41:18,184 --> 00:41:20,978
But every day, there's stuff to do,
and I gotta mow the grass too.

920
00:41:21,061 --> 00:41:22,396
- [Ha-chan] You're a farmer.
- Right.

921
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,273
- Must be super tough.
- [Ruru] Yeah.

922
00:41:24,356 --> 00:41:26,025
- Just one step at a time.
- [Ha-chan] Right.

923
00:41:26,108 --> 00:41:27,651
[Maririn] Takes time to grow.

924
00:41:27,735 --> 00:41:30,404
No one grows up overnight,
or gets stronger overnight.

925
00:41:30,488 --> 00:41:33,199
- [Ha-chan] That's true.
- Yeah. Everyone starts off weak.

926
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:34,992
- Wow, that hit me deep.
- That was really deep.

927
00:41:35,075 --> 00:41:37,119
- [Ruru] Really.
- [Hentona] Hang in there.

928
00:41:37,203 --> 00:41:38,579
"Hang in there" hit me too.

929
00:41:38,662 --> 00:41:41,081
I want his number so I can call him
every day, to ask for advice.

930
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,583
- I'll tell you later.
- [laughing]

931
00:41:42,666 --> 00:41:44,919
- [Maririn] Oh, man.
- [Ruru] I want him to tell me.

932
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:47,213
You boys seem to have a lot of stamina.

933
00:41:47,296 --> 00:41:49,256
- Digging a hole sound good?
- Yes, sir.

934
00:42:01,894 --> 00:42:04,146
- [chuckles] It looks hard.
- [laughs]

935
00:42:05,231 --> 00:42:07,900
- [Nagano] <i>It's like an escape tunnel.</i>
- [Megumi laughs]

936
00:42:08,567 --> 00:42:12,029
[Nagano]<i> Is this an escape attempt?</i>
<i>The security guys need to catch them.</i>

937
00:42:12,112 --> 00:42:14,448
- [Megumi]<i> That's not happening.</i>
- It's hot.

938
00:42:15,074 --> 00:42:16,116
This is tough.

939
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:20,579
[Hentona] Three a day.
One meter by one meter by one meter.

940
00:42:20,663 --> 00:42:24,041
Over the past four years,
I've dug 500 holes, just like these.

941
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,210
- Five hundred?
- Five hundred.

942
00:42:26,293 --> 00:42:27,878
This is what I do every day.

943
00:42:28,796 --> 00:42:29,672
Super early.

944
00:42:29,755 --> 00:42:30,798
We're halfway there.

945
00:42:30,881 --> 00:42:32,091
- [Hentona] Halfway?
- Yeah.

946
00:42:32,174 --> 00:42:33,300
- Fifty centimeters?
- Yeah.

947
00:42:33,384 --> 00:42:34,927
- Yeah, we're there.
- You've worked hard.

948
00:42:35,678 --> 00:42:38,681
- [Nagano]<i> Kazu-kun's doing great.</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Kazu-kun does his share of work.</i>

949
00:42:39,306 --> 00:42:41,976
So do all you guys
have construction experience?

950
00:42:42,059 --> 00:42:44,395
- Yes, in scaffolding. I was a scaffolder.
- A scaffolder.

951
00:42:44,478 --> 00:42:46,105
I did paving. Asphalt.

952
00:42:46,188 --> 00:42:47,565
Oh, okay, yeah.

953
00:42:47,648 --> 00:42:50,317
Kazuma's the same as me,
used to be a scaffolder.

954
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:51,694
- Oh, as well? I see.
- Yes.

955
00:42:51,777 --> 00:42:53,571
- You did demolition, right, Asuka?
- Uh-huh.

956
00:42:54,113 --> 00:42:55,197
- [Ma-kun] Really?
- Really.

957
00:42:55,281 --> 00:42:57,032
- [Ma-kun] Bingo.
- It was amazing.

958
00:42:57,658 --> 00:42:58,492
[Leo] All right.

959
00:42:58,576 --> 00:43:02,204
[Hentona] We're gonna plant a banana tree
here to commemorate everybody here.

960
00:43:02,288 --> 00:43:03,455
- [Ma-kun] Nice.
- [Leo] All right!

961
00:43:03,539 --> 00:43:06,041
- It's born. [laughs]
- [Maririn] Oh, wow.

962
00:43:06,125 --> 00:43:08,127
- All right!
- That was so cool.

963
00:43:08,210 --> 00:43:09,628
[Assun] You did a great job.

964
00:43:10,546 --> 00:43:13,340
- [all] Ooh!
- [Ma-kun] Nice.

965
00:43:13,424 --> 00:43:15,050
- All right, we're done.
- Okay.

966
00:43:15,134 --> 00:43:16,802
- You worked hard today.
- Thank you very much.

967
00:43:16,885 --> 00:43:17,886
Thank you very much.

968
00:43:18,387 --> 00:43:20,472
- [Leo] <i>Joto</i> banana?
- [Ma-kun] <i>Joto</i> banana.

969
00:43:20,556 --> 00:43:23,267
- [Ruru] We're calling it <i>Joto</i> Banana?
- [Ma-kun] You don't like the name?

970
00:43:23,350 --> 00:43:24,226
[Ruru] It's good.

971
00:43:24,310 --> 00:43:25,769
- Let's eat!
- Let's eat.

972
00:43:26,478 --> 00:43:28,856
- [Hentona] High-class banana.
- [Maririn] It's delicious.

973
00:43:28,939 --> 00:43:31,483
- I have 13 varieties at the farm.
- [Ha-chan] So tasty.

974
00:43:31,567 --> 00:43:35,112
[Hentona] Apple banana,
ice-cream banana, Namwa banana.

975
00:43:35,195 --> 00:43:37,573
- This is the legendary banana.
- [Ruru] Huh?

976
00:43:37,656 --> 00:43:39,575
Is that the one you can only get here?

977
00:43:39,658 --> 00:43:41,660
- [Hentona] Exactly.
- [Maririn] You taste that?

978
00:43:41,744 --> 00:43:43,704
- This is good.
- [Assun] I want to try that one.

979
00:43:43,787 --> 00:43:45,623
- [Ma-kun] This is so good.
- [Hentona] This one here.

980
00:43:45,706 --> 00:43:48,167
[Hentona] I think that
being a yankii builds grit.

981
00:43:48,250 --> 00:43:49,710
Especially for boys.

982
00:43:49,793 --> 00:43:50,794
It builds courage.

983
00:43:52,129 --> 00:43:55,966
I was in a biker gang before.
I was in a biker gang in the 1980s.

984
00:43:56,508 --> 00:43:59,094
I was a troublemaker like you
when I was young.

985
00:43:59,178 --> 00:44:00,804
Our gang had 1,000 members.

986
00:44:00,888 --> 00:44:02,389
- You were?
- [Hentona] Right.

987
00:44:02,473 --> 00:44:05,184
Yeah, I was a troublemaker like you
when I was young,

988
00:44:05,267 --> 00:44:08,103
always getting into fights
and doing whatever I wanted.

989
00:44:08,187 --> 00:44:09,813
But nothing comes from fighting.

990
00:44:10,397 --> 00:44:12,358
In the end, love is always stronger.

991
00:44:13,442 --> 00:44:16,945
I'll be straight with you.
The kindest man is the coolest.

992
00:44:17,029 --> 00:44:20,032
And you must never be violent
toward women. You understand?

993
00:44:20,574 --> 00:44:22,576
There's nothing worse. Okay?

994
00:44:22,660 --> 00:44:24,787
Hitting a woman
is the worst thing you can do.

995
00:44:25,287 --> 00:44:29,249
A man like that needs a lot more training.
Bring him to me, I'll knock him out.

996
00:44:29,333 --> 00:44:30,959
- [Nagano]<i> He's so cool.</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Yeah.</i>

997
00:44:31,043 --> 00:44:34,546
- Can I come back again?
- [Hentona] Come back anytime. Anytime.

998
00:44:34,630 --> 00:44:36,674
Really. If you loved it here, come back.

999
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:40,427
It seems people were more violent
in the past.

1000
00:44:40,511 --> 00:44:41,804
Like in the Showa era.

1001
00:44:41,887 --> 00:44:44,181
So it's cool that
he's saying things like that anyway.

1002
00:44:44,264 --> 00:44:46,350
He said we could come back anytime.

1003
00:44:47,017 --> 00:44:50,145
I don't have a home to go back to,
so it made me really happy.

1004
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:53,565
I want to see him again.
He gives me good energy.

1005
00:44:54,858 --> 00:44:57,236
- Has she fallen in love with him?
- [Megumi] Fallen in love…

1006
00:44:57,319 --> 00:45:00,823
[laughing] Wait a minute.
Do we have another participant?

1007
00:45:00,906 --> 00:45:02,616
- Yes.
- Someone of his age?

1008
00:45:02,699 --> 00:45:04,868
- A transfer student.
- [Megumi] We have a transfer student.

1009
00:45:04,952 --> 00:45:07,037
She really opened up to Mr. Hentona.

1010
00:45:07,121 --> 00:45:09,748
Is there a possibility
of her going for Mr. Hentona?

1011
00:45:09,832 --> 00:45:11,917
- [laughing] I don't know.
- [Nagano] Like…

1012
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:15,546
I thought this was just them
spending time on a banana farm.

1013
00:45:15,629 --> 00:45:17,631
I thought he was just meant
to be a nice uncle.

1014
00:45:17,714 --> 00:45:19,216
- Don't let your guard down.
- [Awich] Mmm.

1015
00:45:19,299 --> 00:45:22,136
- Can't help let your guard down with him.
- Don't let your guard down, Nagano.

1016
00:45:22,219 --> 00:45:23,512
This is <i>Badly in Love!</i>

1017
00:45:23,595 --> 00:45:27,391
I really don't want to see Mr. Hentona
bringing his male energy.

1018
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:29,810
We might end up seeing Mr. Hentona
in the sauna.

1019
00:45:29,893 --> 00:45:31,687
- We might.
- [Nagano] Mr. Hentona's--

1020
00:45:31,770 --> 00:45:33,647
We might.
[mimics boy's voice] "It's sauna time."

1021
00:45:33,730 --> 00:45:34,731
[Nagano] "Sauna time," and?

1022
00:45:34,815 --> 00:45:37,276
"The person
who worked the hardest, Mr. Hentona."

1023
00:45:37,359 --> 00:45:40,237
- [all laugh]
- "Mr. Hentona."

1024
00:45:41,071 --> 00:45:43,198
[Tai-chan] Hello. Nice to meet you.

1025
00:45:43,282 --> 00:45:44,616
[Hikaru] It's so cute!

1026
00:45:45,409 --> 00:45:46,869
What is this, like a park?

1027
00:45:46,952 --> 00:45:48,245
[relaxing music playing]

1028
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:49,997
[Tai-chan] Wow.

1029
00:45:53,208 --> 00:45:54,877
Say, "Wassup."

1030
00:45:55,961 --> 00:45:58,422
- Finally, we got it.
- [Bo] Finally.

1031
00:45:59,339 --> 00:46:01,592
Wow, this is actually fun.

1032
00:46:03,510 --> 00:46:04,553
Whoa-ho-ho.

1033
00:46:05,387 --> 00:46:06,513
It's so much fun.

1034
00:46:08,015 --> 00:46:09,725
[laughs]

1035
00:46:10,767 --> 00:46:12,269
[Ari] It's really difficult.

1036
00:46:13,854 --> 00:46:16,482
- I mean, like, my love for you.
- [Hikaru] Mmm.

1037
00:46:16,565 --> 00:46:18,567
I feel like it's not getting through.

1038
00:46:19,610 --> 00:46:21,195
I keep asking you questions like,

1039
00:46:21,278 --> 00:46:23,405
"How are you?"
"Are you interested in anybody?"

1040
00:46:23,489 --> 00:46:24,323
[Hikaru] Mmm.

1041
00:46:24,865 --> 00:46:26,492
And when I ask you those things,

1042
00:46:26,992 --> 00:46:30,078
you're always like, "No,
I'm not interested in anybody yet."

1043
00:46:30,621 --> 00:46:34,500
But you have to be interested in somebody
before you start liking them, right?

1044
00:46:34,583 --> 00:46:37,252
You know, we're already
halfway through our time here,

1045
00:46:37,336 --> 00:46:41,006
and you tell me you're still
not interested in anybody, so I'm like…

1046
00:46:41,089 --> 00:46:44,176
I feel like it's going to drag on,
and we'll run out of time.

1047
00:46:44,259 --> 00:46:47,471
You know, like, am I making
any progress with you?

1048
00:46:47,554 --> 00:46:49,598
- [Hikaru] Mmm.
- I'm starting to feel anxious.

1049
00:46:49,681 --> 00:46:52,434
[Hikaru] So, honestly,
literally, just yesterday,

1050
00:46:52,518 --> 00:46:54,937
I made up my mind and decided

1051
00:46:55,020 --> 00:46:57,898
to focus only on you
and Tai-chan going forward.

1052
00:46:57,981 --> 00:46:58,815
Mmm-hmm.

1053
00:46:59,399 --> 00:47:01,360
And I do have a reason for that.

1054
00:47:02,069 --> 00:47:04,780
I found out about the time
that Bo hit a girl.

1055
00:47:05,697 --> 00:47:08,116
I don't think you can come back from that.

1056
00:47:08,200 --> 00:47:11,328
That was a dealbreaker for me,
so I knew I wasn't gonna go for Bo.

1057
00:47:13,539 --> 00:47:16,375
And I was planning on
telling him that today.

1058
00:47:16,875 --> 00:47:21,547
Well, I'm glad to hear
that you're going to focus on us two,

1059
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:24,841
and that you might turn down Bo
and consider me and Taisei.

1060
00:47:25,717 --> 00:47:26,885
I'm happy to hear that.

1061
00:47:31,139 --> 00:47:31,974
[Bo] Hey.

1062
00:47:32,599 --> 00:47:35,185
- What's up?
- You two should talk.

1063
00:47:35,769 --> 00:47:37,980
I've got an iced tea with my name on it.

1064
00:47:38,063 --> 00:47:39,982
[Bo chuckles] Okay. What's up?

1065
00:47:40,065 --> 00:47:42,568
[Hikaru] Well,
we're halfway through, aren't we?

1066
00:47:42,651 --> 00:47:44,236
- [Bo] Yeah, we are.
- [Hikaru] Right.

1067
00:47:44,945 --> 00:47:45,946
[Nagano]<i> Is she gonna do it?</i>

1068
00:47:46,572 --> 00:47:48,490
Well, when it comes to you,

1069
00:47:48,574 --> 00:47:50,409
I was planning on telling you,

1070
00:47:50,492 --> 00:47:53,287
or, actually asking you
about something today.

1071
00:47:53,370 --> 00:47:55,372
- You were? Okay.
- Mmm-hmm.

1072
00:47:55,455 --> 00:47:58,667
I heard that you have hit a woman before.

1073
00:47:58,750 --> 00:47:59,585
Mmm.

1074
00:47:59,668 --> 00:48:03,630
So, my dad was
really, really abusive towards me.

1075
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:07,009
- He wouldn't hit me 'cause I'd been bad--
- He'd just do it randomly?

1076
00:48:07,092 --> 00:48:09,553
He'd hit me if I didn't give him a massage
when he told me to.

1077
00:48:09,636 --> 00:48:10,721
Unreasonable.

1078
00:48:10,804 --> 00:48:13,307
And so, for me,

1079
00:48:14,099 --> 00:48:15,934
no matter what the girl did,

1080
00:48:16,476 --> 00:48:18,562
I think that I just couldn't…

1081
00:48:19,229 --> 00:48:21,607
be with a guy who'd ever hit a girl.

1082
00:48:22,441 --> 00:48:23,275
Mmm.

1083
00:48:23,775 --> 00:48:27,863
And so, as of yesterday,
I thought I couldn't be with you.

1084
00:48:27,946 --> 00:48:28,947
But today…

1085
00:48:30,532 --> 00:48:33,035
All four of us went out together.

1086
00:48:34,077 --> 00:48:36,163
And, like, you know…

1087
00:48:37,372 --> 00:48:40,334
Now all I can see
is the positive side of you.

1088
00:48:40,417 --> 00:48:43,086
- [Nagano]<i> What?</i>
- And I think that you're really…

1089
00:48:44,004 --> 00:48:46,214
- You have really good qualities.
- Mmm.

1090
00:48:46,757 --> 00:48:49,593
And you actually have good qualities

1091
00:48:49,676 --> 00:48:52,179
that neither Ari nor Tai-chan has.

1092
00:48:52,262 --> 00:48:53,096
Hmm.

1093
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:54,931
I thought you were going to turn me down.

1094
00:48:55,015 --> 00:48:55,849
Hmm.

1095
00:48:56,850 --> 00:48:59,019
- I just wanted to make it clear.
- Hmm.

1096
00:48:59,853 --> 00:49:02,230
I just wanted to be very clear.

1097
00:49:07,486 --> 00:49:09,446
- She's stringing him along.
- [Megumi] Hmm.

1098
00:49:09,529 --> 00:49:12,324
Huh? That's totally different
to what she said to Ari.

1099
00:49:12,407 --> 00:49:14,076
You know they'll find out later?

1100
00:49:17,579 --> 00:49:21,083
I won't be able to know everything
about your past.

1101
00:49:21,166 --> 00:49:23,585
I mean, you are similar in a way, but…

1102
00:49:24,461 --> 00:49:25,295
[Tai-chan] Not yet?

1103
00:49:25,379 --> 00:49:26,630
- [gasps] Whoa.
- More time?

1104
00:49:27,547 --> 00:49:28,840
- You scared me.
- Not enough time.

1105
00:49:28,924 --> 00:49:31,468
- Not enough?
- No, like, not enough time overall.

1106
00:49:32,094 --> 00:49:33,512
- I want us to talk too.
- Mm-hmm.

1107
00:49:34,388 --> 00:49:35,389
[Bo] Thanks.

1108
00:49:39,393 --> 00:49:42,145
I'm going to tell each of you
what I think about you.

1109
00:49:42,229 --> 00:49:43,980
Oh, okay, okay, lay it on me.

1110
00:49:44,064 --> 00:49:48,235
- All of you have your flaws.
- Uh-huh. I get that.

1111
00:49:48,318 --> 00:49:50,779
And all of you have
your own good qualities.

1112
00:49:50,862 --> 00:49:52,364
- Yeah, okay.
- Like, naturally.

1113
00:49:52,447 --> 00:49:54,282
I already told Ari this but…

1114
00:49:54,366 --> 00:49:55,200
[Tai-chan] Uh-huh.

1115
00:49:55,283 --> 00:49:57,577
…I feel like we would just be friends.

1116
00:49:58,161 --> 00:49:58,995
Okay, I see.

1117
00:49:59,579 --> 00:50:02,582
As for Bo, the domestic violence thing
really bothers me.

1118
00:50:02,666 --> 00:50:05,377
- Oh, I heard a bit about that.
- Yeah, it bothers me.

1119
00:50:05,460 --> 00:50:07,796
And when it comes to you, Tai-chan…

1120
00:50:07,879 --> 00:50:09,339
- Oh, finally.
- [chuckles] Finally, huh?

1121
00:50:09,423 --> 00:50:10,424
Finally, my turn.

1122
00:50:10,507 --> 00:50:11,550
- Finally…
- Yeah.

1123
00:50:11,633 --> 00:50:14,302
- You're like, really mellow, you know?
- Mm-hmm.

1124
00:50:14,386 --> 00:50:16,304
- Like, you're quite soft-spoken.
- I am?

1125
00:50:16,388 --> 00:50:18,181
Mm-hmm. And I didn't like that.

1126
00:50:18,265 --> 00:50:19,641
- Oh, I see.
- But that went away.

1127
00:50:19,725 --> 00:50:21,017
That's not how I am.

1128
00:50:21,643 --> 00:50:23,854
- And so, now, since that went away…
- Mmm.

1129
00:50:25,105 --> 00:50:26,356
So, mmm…

1130
00:50:27,065 --> 00:50:29,025
I see you as the one
who's most like a man.

1131
00:50:29,109 --> 00:50:30,152
[Nagano]<i> What?</i>

1132
00:50:31,486 --> 00:50:33,029
- [giggles]
- What's that?

1133
00:50:33,655 --> 00:50:36,241
I see you as the one
who's most like a man.

1134
00:50:38,910 --> 00:50:41,204
I thought so. I'm kidding, I'm kidding.

1135
00:50:41,288 --> 00:50:42,956
- But honestly…
- [Hikaru] But, like, mm…

1136
00:50:43,707 --> 00:50:45,250
Honestly, thank you for that.

1137
00:50:45,333 --> 00:50:48,545
And I think you're also
totally my type, looks-wise.

1138
00:50:48,628 --> 00:50:49,671
- Who, me?
- Your clothes.

1139
00:50:49,755 --> 00:50:50,589
Oh, really?

1140
00:50:50,672 --> 00:50:55,302
When I see you with your guy friends,
I just think you seem really cool.

1141
00:50:55,385 --> 00:50:57,262
- Like, when you're laughing.
- Yeah, I am cool.

1142
00:50:57,345 --> 00:50:59,681
- Yeah.
- Like Ari, he's so loud.

1143
00:50:59,765 --> 00:51:02,100
- [laughs]
- I can't understand what he's saying.

1144
00:51:02,768 --> 00:51:04,728
Hikaru!

1145
00:51:06,271 --> 00:51:08,690
[Tai-chan] I'm glad you've been
so straightforward with me.

1146
00:51:09,524 --> 00:51:11,151
I didn't want
to make you talk for too long

1147
00:51:11,234 --> 00:51:14,279
'cause that might make you tired,
and I wanted to hear your honest opinion.

1148
00:51:14,988 --> 00:51:16,615
I don't know, I'm pretty stoked.

1149
00:51:18,158 --> 00:51:21,161
I always knew that I would beat the others
and win you in the end.

1150
00:51:22,370 --> 00:51:24,122
- I really did.
- [giggles]

1151
00:51:24,206 --> 00:51:25,207
I knew it all along.

1152
00:51:29,336 --> 00:51:30,462
So it's me, after all.

1153
00:51:34,257 --> 00:51:36,927
This is where I want to hear
the detective's opinion.

1154
00:51:37,010 --> 00:51:39,763
Why do you think Hikaru
said those things to the three of them?

1155
00:51:39,846 --> 00:51:41,139
What do you think she's thinking?

1156
00:51:41,223 --> 00:51:43,308
Well, being popular,

1157
00:51:43,391 --> 00:51:45,393
- it feels good, doesn't it?
- [Nagano] It does feel good.

1158
00:51:45,477 --> 00:51:47,354
- And she's the most popular.
- [Nagano] Yeah.

1159
00:51:47,437 --> 00:51:51,483
So she's probably hoping and trying to
keep this going for as long as possible.

1160
00:51:51,566 --> 00:51:52,442
I see.

1161
00:51:52,526 --> 00:51:56,655
But if she keeps doing that,
she's going to pay for it later on.

1162
00:51:56,738 --> 00:51:57,948
- Right?
- [Megumi] Right.

1163
00:51:59,199 --> 00:52:00,992
- [Ma-kun] Let's go have a smoke.
- [Assun] Let's go.

1164
00:52:02,327 --> 00:52:06,289
I'm so scared about checking
my phone after all this is over.

1165
00:52:06,373 --> 00:52:08,250
[Ma-kun] Me too. I feel the same way.

1166
00:52:08,333 --> 00:52:11,044
Reality is going to hit us,
like, super hard.

1167
00:52:11,127 --> 00:52:13,964
Yeah. But that's what helped me
make up my mind just now.

1168
00:52:15,465 --> 00:52:16,633
I'm gonna be with you.

1169
00:52:17,467 --> 00:52:18,385
Be with me?

1170
00:52:21,388 --> 00:52:23,515
- No matter what.
- Wanna kiss?

1171
00:52:24,057 --> 00:52:25,100
- [Nagano]<i> What?</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Oh!</i>

1172
00:52:25,183 --> 00:52:26,434
Won't they expel us?

1173
00:52:26,518 --> 00:52:28,854
- Yeah.
- [both laugh]

1174
00:52:31,314 --> 00:52:33,316
[clears throat] I mean,

1175
00:52:33,400 --> 00:52:36,111
I've never really trusted people,
not really,

1176
00:52:36,903 --> 00:52:38,780
- 'cause I'm scared of getting betrayed.
- Mmm-hmm.

1177
00:52:38,864 --> 00:52:40,532
But I don't mind it if you do it.

1178
00:52:41,074 --> 00:52:42,325
I wanna experience it.

1179
00:52:43,368 --> 00:52:44,244
Betrayal.

1180
00:52:44,744 --> 00:52:47,664
- You're really saying that?
- Yeah.

1181
00:52:49,249 --> 00:52:50,792
Because I honestly don't know.

1182
00:52:52,085 --> 00:52:53,628
You're leaving it up to me?

1183
00:52:54,296 --> 00:52:55,755
No, it's not that.

1184
00:52:55,839 --> 00:52:58,383
- I'm just saying--
- But I've been sharing…

1185
00:53:02,804 --> 00:53:04,806
my feelings for you, and you just…

1186
00:53:08,768 --> 00:53:09,936
I made a mistake.

1187
00:53:10,020 --> 00:53:13,148
Yeah, I don't deserve
to be told that in an angry tone.

1188
00:53:13,231 --> 00:53:14,190
I've been more…

1189
00:53:14,858 --> 00:53:18,194
I've been more upfront than you
about my feelings.

1190
00:53:20,488 --> 00:53:22,908
Forget what I just said. I made a mistake.

1191
00:53:24,784 --> 00:53:28,663
[Assun]<i> After the first letter,</i>
<i>it's basically been one-sided on my part.</i>

1192
00:53:28,747 --> 00:53:30,373
<i>He hasn't made as much effort.</i>

1193
00:53:30,957 --> 00:53:33,585
I sent him a letter,
and I won the girls' competition

1194
00:53:33,668 --> 00:53:35,420
and chose him and went on a date.

1195
00:53:36,212 --> 00:53:39,132
So if he keeps, like, not reciprocating,

1196
00:53:39,215 --> 00:53:43,345
if he doesn't show me any affection,
then I'll be like…

1197
00:53:44,262 --> 00:53:46,181
maybe I should just give up on it.

1198
00:53:47,849 --> 00:53:49,768
We feel like you want
to keep both of us around.

1199
00:53:49,851 --> 00:53:51,519
That's the one thing I didn't want.

1200
00:53:51,603 --> 00:53:54,522
And what we're saying is that
that's what it looks like.

1201
00:53:55,565 --> 00:53:58,234
- [Nagano]<i> What?</i>
- [Megumi]<i> Oh, my.</i>

1202
00:53:58,318 --> 00:54:00,111
[sobbing]

1203
00:54:02,864 --> 00:54:05,367
- Wait, no. What? What's going on?
- [Megumi] Oh, no.

1204
00:54:05,450 --> 00:54:06,660
Would you cry that much?

1205
00:54:07,327 --> 00:54:09,454
Wait, hold on, what was that at the end?

1206
00:54:10,538 --> 00:54:12,791
Maybe Mr. Hentona appeared or something?

1207
00:54:13,833 --> 00:54:15,418
- [gasps]
- Maybe he was really scared.

1208
00:54:15,502 --> 00:54:18,630
- All like, "I'm so scared!" and crying?
- [Nagano] He's like, "I'm so scared!"

1209
00:54:18,713 --> 00:54:21,424
- You suck at watching dating shows.
- [all laughing]

1210
00:54:22,384 --> 00:54:24,386
[closing theme song playing]
